<?xml version="1.0"?>
<body language="English">
	<row id="msg_0803_00000" index="0">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">garbage</attribute>
		<language name="English"></language>
		<language name="日本語"></language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00001" index="1">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The seed on its back is filled\nwith nutrients. The seed grows\nsteadily larger as its body grows.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00002" index="2">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Exposure to sunlight adds to its\nstrength. Sunlight also makes the\nbud on its back grow larger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00003" index="3">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By spreading the broad petals of\nits flower and catching the sun’s\nrays, it fills its body with power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00004" index="4">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The flame on its tail shows the\nstrength of its life force. If it is weak,\nthe flame also burns weakly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00005" index="5">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is very hotheaded by nature,\nso it constantly seeks opponents.\nIt calms down only when it wins.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00006" index="6">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If CHARIZARD becomes furious,\nthe flame at the tip of its tail flares\nup in a light blue shade.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00007" index="7">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The shell is soft when it is born.\nIt soon becomes so resilient,\nprodding fingers will bounce off it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00008" index="8">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is a well-established symbol of\nlongevity. If its shell has algae on it,\nthat WARTORTLE is very old.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00009" index="9">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It deliberately makes itself heavy\nso it can withstand the recoil\nof the water jets it fires.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00010" index="10">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For protection, it releases a horrible\nstench from the antennae on its\nhead to drive away enemies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00011" index="11">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Inside the shell, it is soft and\nweak as it prepares to evolve.\nIt stays motionless in the shell.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00012" index="12">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It collects honey every day. It rubs\nhoney onto the hairs on its legs\nto carry it back to its nest.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00013" index="13">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its poison stinger is very powerful.\nIts bright-colored body is intended\nto warn off its enemies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00014" index="14">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Although it is a cocoon, it can\nmove a little. It can extend its\npoison barb if it is attacked.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00015" index="15">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can take down any opponent with\nits powerful poison stingers.\nIt sometimes attacks in swarms.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00016" index="16">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It usually hides in tall grass.\nBecause it dislikes fighting,\nit protects itself by kicking up sand.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00017" index="17">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has outstanding vision. However\nhigh it flies, it is able to distinguish\nthe movements of its prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00018" index="18">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its well-developed chest muscles make\nit strong enough to whip up a gusty\nwindstorm with just a few flaps.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00019" index="19">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It eats anything. Wherever food is\navailable, it will settle down and\nproduce offspring continuously.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00020" index="20">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Gnaws on anything with its tough\nfangs. It can even topple concrete\nbuildings by gnawing on them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00021" index="21">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flaps its short wings to flush out\ninsects from tall grass. It then\nplucks them with its stubby beak.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00022" index="22">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shoots itself suddenly high into\nthe sky, then plummets down in\none fell swoop to strike its prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00023" index="23">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can freely detach its jaw to\nswallow large prey whole. It can\nbecome too heavy to move, however.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00024" index="24">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Transfixing prey with the face-like\npattern on its belly, it binds\nand poisons the frightened victim.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00025" index="25">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon roasts\nhard berries with electricity to\nmake them tender enough to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00026" index="26">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its electricity builds, its\nmuscles are stimulated, and it becomes\nmore aggressive than usual.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00027" index="27">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it fell from a great height, this\nPokémon could save itself by rolling\ninto a ball and bouncing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00028" index="28">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In an attempt to hide itself,\nit will run around at top speed to\nkick up a blinding dust storm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00029" index="29">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The poison hidden in its small horn\nis extremely potent. Even a tiny\nscratch can have fatal results.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00030" index="30">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When feeding its young, it first\nchews the food into a paste, then\nspits it out for the offspring.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00031" index="31">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is covered with needle-like\nscales. It never shows signs\nof shrinking from any attack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00032" index="32">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is small, but its horn is filled\nwith poison. It charges then stabs\nwith the horn to inject poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00033" index="33">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It raises its big ears to check its\nsurroundings. If it senses anything,\nit attacks immediately.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00034" index="34">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It swings its big tail around during\nbattle. If its foe flinches, it will\ncharge with its sturdy body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00035" index="35">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The moonlight that it stores in the\nwings on its back apparently gives\nit the ability to float in midair.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00036" index="36">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With its acute hearing, it can\npick up sounds from far away.\nIt usually hides in quiet places.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00037" index="37">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it develops, its single white\ntail gains color and splits into six.\nIt is quite warm and cuddly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00038" index="38">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Some legends claim that each of its\nnine tails has its own unique type\nof special mystical power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00039" index="39">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it inflates to sing a lullaby,\nit can perform longer and cause\nsure drowsiness in its audience.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00040" index="40">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their fur feels so good that if two\nof them snuggle together,\nthey won’t want to be separated.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00041" index="41">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">While flying, it constantly emits\nultrasonic waves from its mouth to\ncheck its surroundings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00042" index="42">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">However hard its victim’s hide may be,\nit punctures with sharp fangs\nand gorges itself with blood.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00043" index="43">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Awakened by moonlight, it roams\nactively at night. In the day, it stays\nquietly underground.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00044" index="44">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">What appears to be drool is actually\nsweet honey. It is very sticky and\nclings stubbornly if touched.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00045" index="45">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the world’s largest petals.\nWith every step, the petals shake\nout heavy clouds of toxic pollen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00046" index="46">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is doused with mushroom spores\nwhen it is born. As its body grows,\nmushrooms sprout from its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00047" index="47">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stays mostly in dark, damp places,\nthe preference not of the bug, but\nof the big mushroom on its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00048" index="48">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its eyes also function as radar\nunits. It catches and eats small\nbugs that hide in darkness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00049" index="49">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it attacks, it flaps its large\nwings violently to scatter its\npoisonous powder all around.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00050" index="50">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its skin is very thin. If it is exposed\nto light, its blood heats up,\ncausing it to grow weak.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00051" index="51">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its three heads bob separately up\nand down to loosen the soil nearby,\nmaking it easier for it to burrow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00052" index="52">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is fascinated by round objects.\nIt can’t stop playing with them\nuntil it tires and falls asleep.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00053" index="53">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Many adore it for its sophisticated air.\nHowever, it will lash out and\nscratch for little reason.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00054" index="54">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has mystical powers but doesn’t\nrecall that it has used them.\nThat is why it always looks puzzled.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00055" index="55">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it swims at full speed using\nits long, webbed limbs, its forehead\nsomehow begins to glow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00056" index="56">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is extremely ill-tempered.\nGroups of them will attack any\nhandy target for no reason.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00057" index="57">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If approached while asleep,\nit may awaken and angrily give chase\nin a groggy state of semi-sleep.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00058" index="58">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a brave and trustworthy\nnature. It fearlessly stands up\nto bigger and stronger foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00059" index="59">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary Chinese Pokémon is\nconsidered magnificent. Many people\nare enchanted by its grand mane.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00060" index="60">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because it is inept at walking on\nits newly grown legs, it always \nswims around in water.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00061" index="61">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The swirl on its belly subtly undulates.\nStaring at it may gradually\ncause drowsiness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00062" index="62">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This strong and skilled swimmer is\neven capable of crossing the\nPacific Ocean just by kicking.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00063" index="63">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It senses impending attacks and\nteleports away to safety before the\nactual attacks can strike.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00064" index="64">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It possesses strong spiritual power.\nThe more danger it faces,\nthe stronger its psychic power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00065" index="65">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Closing both its eyes heightens all\nits other senses. This enables it to\nuse its abilities to their extremes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00066" index="66">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Always brimming with power,\nit passes time by lifting boulders.\nDoing so makes it even stronger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00067" index="67">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It always goes at its full power,\nbut this very tough and durable\nPokémon never gets tired.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00068" index="68">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It quickly swings its four arms to\nrock its opponents with ceaseless\npunches and chops from all angles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00069" index="69">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Even though its body is extremely\nskinny, it is blindingly fast\nwhen catching its prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00070" index="70">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Even though it is filled with acid,\nit does not melt because it also\noozes a protective fluid.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00071" index="71">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Acid that has dissolved many prey\nbecomes sweeter, making it even\nmore effective at attracting prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00072" index="72">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the tide goes out, dehydrated\nTENTACOOL remains can be found\nwashed up on the shore.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00073" index="73">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its 80 tentacles absorb water and\nstretch almost endlessly to\nconstrict its prey and enemies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00074" index="74">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Most people may not notice,\nbut a closer look should reveal that\nthere are many GEODUDE around.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00075" index="75">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With a free and uncaring nature,\nit doesn’t mind if pieces break off\nwhile it rolls down mountains.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00076" index="76">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sheds its skin once a year.\nThe discarded shell immediately\nhardens and crumbles away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00077" index="77">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is a weak runner immediately\nafter birth. It gradually becomes\nfaster by chasing after its parents.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00078" index="78">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">At full gallop, its four hooves\nbarely touch the ground because\nit moves so incredibly fast.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00079" index="79">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lazes vacantly near water.\nIf something bites its tail, it won’t\neven notice for a whole day.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00080" index="80">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If the tail-biting SHELLDER is thrown\noff in a harsh battle, it reverts to\nbeing an ordinary SLOWPOKE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00081" index="81">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is attracted by electromagnetic\nwaves. It may approach Trainers\nif they are using their Pokégear.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00082" index="82">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Three MAGNEMITE are linked by a\nstrong magnetic force. Earaches\nwill occur if you get too close.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00083" index="83">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If anyone tries to disturb where the\nessential plant stalks grow, it uses its\nown stalk to thwart them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00084" index="84">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By alternately raising and lowering\nits two heads, it balances itself\nto be more stable while running.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00085" index="85">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It collects data and plans three times\nas wisely, but it may think too much\nand fall into a state of immobility.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00086" index="86">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Although it can’t walk well on land,\nit is a graceful swimmer. It especially\nloves being in frigid seas.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00087" index="87">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its streamlined body has little\ndrag in water. The colder the\ntemperature, the friskier it gets.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00088" index="88">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it moves, it loses bits of its body,\nfrom which new GRIMER emerge.\nThis worsens the stench around it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00089" index="89">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They love to gather in smelly areas\nwhere sludge accumulates, making\nthe stench around them worse.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00090" index="90">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It swims facing backward by opening\nand closing its two-piece shell.\nIt is surprisingly fast.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00091" index="91">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Once it slams its shell shut,\nit is impossible to open, even by\nthose with superior strength.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00092" index="92">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With its gas-like body, it can sneak\ninto any place it desires. However,\nit can be blown away by wind.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00093" index="93">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In total darkness, where nothing is\nvisible, HAUNTER lurks, silently\nstalking its next victim.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00094" index="94">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It steals heat from its surroundings.\nIf you feel a sudden chill,\nit is certain that a GENGAR appeared.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00095" index="95">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It twists and squirms through\nthe ground. The thunderous roar of\nits tunneling echoes a long way.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00096" index="96">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If you think that you had a good dream\nbut you can’t remember it,\na DROWZEE has probably eaten it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00097" index="97">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it is very hungry, it puts\nhumans it meets to sleep,\nthen it feasts on their dreams.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00098" index="98">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it senses danger approaching,\nit cloaks itself with bubbles from\nits mouth so it will look bigger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00099" index="99">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can hardly lift its massive,\novergrown pincer. The pincer’s size\nmakes it difficult to aim properly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00100" index="100">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It rolls to move. If the ground is\nuneven, a sudden jolt from hitting\na bump can cause it to explode.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00101" index="101">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is dangerous. If it has too much\nelectricity and has nothing to do,\nit amuses itself by exploding.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00102" index="102">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their shells are very durable. Even if\nthey crack, they can survive without\nspilling their contents.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00103" index="103">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its three heads think independently.\nHowever, they are friendly and\nnever appear to squabble.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00104" index="104">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it is sad or lonely, the skull\nit wears shakes and emits a plaintive\nand mournful sound.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00105" index="105">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has been seen pounding boulders\nwith the bone it carries in order\nto tap out messages to others.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00106" index="106">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This amazing Pokémon has an awesome\nsense of balance. It can kick in\nsuccession from any position.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00107" index="107">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its punches slice the air. However,\nit seems to need a short break after\nfighting for three minutes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00108" index="108">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its tongue has well-developed\nnerves that run to the very tip,\nso it can be deftly manipulated.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00109" index="109">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its thin, filmy body is filled\nwith gases that cause constant\nsniffles, coughs and teary eyes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00110" index="110">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If one of the twin KOFFING inflates,\nthe other one deflates. It constantly\nmixes its poisonous gases.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00111" index="111">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is inept at turning because of\nits four short legs. It can only\ncharge and run in one direction.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00112" index="112">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its rugged hide protects it from\neven the heat of lava. However,\nthe hide also makes it insensitive.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00113" index="113">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It walks carefully to prevent its\negg from breaking. However,\nit is extremely fast at running away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00114" index="114">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The vines that cloak its entire\nbody are always jiggling.\nThey effectively unnerve its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00115" index="115">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it is safe, the young gets out of\nthe belly pouch to play. The adult\nkeeps a close eye on the youngster.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00116" index="116">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If attacked by a larger enemy,\nit quickly swims to safety by adeptly\ncontrolling its well-developed dorsal fin.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00117" index="117">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An examination of its cells revealed\nthe presence of a gene not found in\nHORSEA. It became a hot topic.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00118" index="118">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its dorsal, pectoral and tail fins\nwave elegantly in water. That is why\nit is known as the water dancer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00119" index="119">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">During spawning season, SEAKING\ngather from all over, causing rivers to\nappear a brilliant red.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00120" index="120">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">At night, the middle of its body\nslowly flickers with the same\nrhythm as a human heartbeat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00121" index="121">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The middle section of its body is\ncalled the core. It glows in a\ndifferent color each time it is seen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00122" index="122">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A skilled mime from birth,\nit gains the ability to create\ninvisible objects as it matures.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00123" index="123">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It slashes through grass with its\nsharp scythes, moving too fast\nfor the human eye to track.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00124" index="124">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It rocks its body rhythmically.\nIt appears to alter the rhythm\ndepending on how it is feeling.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00125" index="125">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Electricity runs across the surface\nof its body. In darkness, its entire\nbody glows a whitish-blue.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00126" index="126">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It dislikes cold places, so it blows\nscorching flames to make the\nenvironment suitable for itself.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00127" index="127">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With its pincer horns, it digs burrows\nto sleep in at night. In the morning,\ndamp soil clings to its body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00128" index="128">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They fight each other by locking\nhorns. The herd’s protector takes\npride in its battle-scarred horns.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00129" index="129">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An underpowered, pathetic Pokémon.\nIt may jump high on rare occasions,\nbut usually not more than seven feet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00130" index="130">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They say that during past strife,\nGYARADOS would appear and leave\nblazing ruins in its wake.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00131" index="131">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They have gentle hearts. Because\nthey rarely fight, many have been\ncaught. Their number has dwindled.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00132" index="132">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can transform into anything.\nWhen it sleeps, it changes into a\nstone to avoid being attacked.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00133" index="133">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the ability to alter the\ncomposition of its body to suit its\nsurrounding environment.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00134" index="134">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When VAPOREON’s fins begin to\nvibrate, it is a sign that rain\nwill come within a few hours.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00135" index="135">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It concentrates the weak electric\ncharges emitted by its cells and\nlaunches wicked lightning bolts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00136" index="136">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stores some of the air it inhales in\nits internal flame pouch, which heats it\nto over 3,000 degrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00137" index="137">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is a manmade Pokémon. Since it\ndoesn’t breathe, people are eager\nto try it in any environment.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00138" index="138">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Revived from an ancient fossil,\nthis Pokémon uses air stored in its\nshell to sink and rise in water.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00139" index="139">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Apparently, it cracked SHELLDER’s\nshell with its sharp fangs and\nsucked out the insides.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00140" index="140">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">On rare occasions, some have been\nfound as fossils which they became\nwhile hiding on the ocean floor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00141" index="141">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In the water, it tucks in its limbs\nto become more compact, then it\nwiggles its shell to swim fast.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00142" index="142">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A vicious Pokémon from the distant\npast, it appears to have flown by\nspreading its wings and gliding.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00143" index="143">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">What sounds like its cry may\nactually be its snores or the\nrumblings of its hungry belly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00144" index="144">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The magnificent, seemingly translucent\nwings of this legendary bird Pokémon\nare said to be made of ice.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00145" index="145">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary bird Pokémon\ncauses savage thunderstorms by\nflapping its glittering wings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00146" index="146">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary Pokémon scatters\nembers with every flap of its wings.\nIt is a thrilling sight to behold.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00147" index="147">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is born large to start with.\nIt repeatedly sheds its skin as it\nsteadily grows longer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00148" index="148">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They say that if it emits an aura\nfrom its whole body, the weather\nwill begin to change instantly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00149" index="149">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that this Pokémon constantly\nflies over the immense seas\nand rescues drowning people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00150" index="150">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because its battle abilities were\nraised to the ultimate level,\nit thinks only of defeating its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00151" index="151">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Apparently, it appears only to\nthose people who are pure of heart\nand have a strong desire to see it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00152" index="152">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A sweet aroma gently wafts from\nthe leaf on its head. It is docile\nand loves to soak up sunrays.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00153" index="153">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The scent of spices comes from\naround its neck. Somehow,\nsniffing it makes you want to fight.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00154" index="154">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The aroma that rises from its\npetals contains a substance that\ncalms aggressive feelings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00155" index="155">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is timid, and always curls itself\nup in a ball. If attacked, it\nflares up its back for protection.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00156" index="156">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Be careful if it turns its back\nduring battle. It means that it will\nattack with the fire on its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00157" index="157">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If its rage peaks, it becomes so\nhot that anything that touches it\nwill instantly go up in flames.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00158" index="158">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its powerful, well-developed jaws\nare capable of crushing anything.\nEven its Trainer must be careful.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00159" index="159">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it loses a fang, a new one\ngrows back in its place. There are\nalways 48 fangs lining its mouth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00160" index="160">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it bites with its massive and\npowerful jaws, it shakes its head\nand savagely tears its victim up.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00161" index="161">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very cautious Pokémon, it raises\nitself up using its tail to get a\nbetter view of its surroundings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00162" index="162">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It makes a nest to suit its long and\nskinny body. The nest is impossible\nfor other Pokémon to enter.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00163" index="163">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It always stands on one foot.\nIt changes feet so fast,\nthe movement can rarely be seen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00164" index="164">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its eyes are specially adapted.\nThey concentrate even faint light\nand enable it to see in the dark.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00165" index="165">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is very timid. It will be afraid\nto move if it is alone. But it will\nbe active if it is in a group.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00166" index="166">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the stars flicker in the\nnight sky, it flutters about,\nscattering a glowing powder.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00167" index="167">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lies still in the same pose for\ndays in its web, waiting for its\nunsuspecting prey to wander close.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00168" index="168">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It spins string not only from its\nrear but also from its mouth. It’s\nhard to tell which end is which.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00169" index="169">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flies so silently through the\ndark on its four wings that it may\nnot be noticed even when nearby.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00170" index="170">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shoots positive and negative\nelectricity between the tips of its\ntwo antennae and zaps its enemies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00171" index="171">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The light it emits is so bright that\nit can illuminate the sea’s surface\nfrom a depth of over three miles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00172" index="172">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is not yet skilled at storing\nelectricity. It may send out a\njolt if amused or startled.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00173" index="173">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because of its unusual, starlike\nsilhouette, people believe that\nit came here on a meteor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00174" index="174">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a very soft body. If it\nstarts to roll, it will bounce all\nover and be impossible to stop.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00175" index="175">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The shell seems to be filled with\njoy. It is said that it will share\ngood luck when treated kindly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00176" index="176">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They say that it will appear before\nkindhearted, caring people and\nshower them with happiness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00177" index="177">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because its wings aren’t yet fully\ngrown, it has to hop to get around.\nIt is always staring at something.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00178" index="178">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They say that it stays still and\nquiet because it is seeing both the\npast and future at the same time.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00179" index="179">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If static electricity builds in its\nbody, its fleece doubles in volume.\nTouching it will shock you.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00180" index="180">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As a result of storing too much\nelectricity, it developed patches\nwhere even downy wool won’t grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00181" index="181">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The tail’s tip shines brightly and\ncan be seen from far away. It acts\nas a beacon for lost people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00182" index="182">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">BELLOSSOM gather at times and seem\nto dance. They say that the dance\nis a ritual to summon the sun.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00183" index="183">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The tip of its tail, which contains\noil that is lighter than water,\nlets it swim without drowning.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00184" index="184">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By keeping still and listening\nintently, it can tell what is in even\nwild, fast-moving rivers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00185" index="185">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Although it always pretends to be a\ntree, its composition appears more\nsimilar to rock than to vegetation.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00186" index="186">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If POLIWAG and POLIWHIRL hear its\nechoing cry, they respond by\ngathering from far and wide.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00187" index="187">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To keep from being blown away by\nthe wind, they gather in clusters.\nBut they do enjoy gentle breezes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00188" index="188">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The bloom on top of its head opens\nand closes as the temperature\nfluctuates up and down.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00189" index="189">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Once it catches the wind, it deftly\ncontrols its cotton-puff spores--\nit can even float around the world.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00190" index="190">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its tail is so powerful that it can\nuse it to grab a tree branch and\nhold itself up in the air.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00191" index="191">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It may plummet from the sky.\nIf attacked by a SPEAROW,\nit will violently shake its leaves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00192" index="192">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It converts sunlight into energy.\nIn the darkness after sunset, it\ncloses its petals and becomes still.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00193" index="193">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it flaps its wings really fast,\nit can generate shock waves that\nwill shatter windows in the area.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00194" index="194">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon lives in cold water.\nIt will leave the water to search\nfor food when it gets cold outside.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00195" index="195">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This carefree Pokémon has an\neasy-going nature. While swimming,\nit always bumps into boat hulls.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00196" index="196">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses the fine hair that covers\nits body to sense air currents and\npredict its enemy’s actions.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00197" index="197">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When agitated, this Pokémon\nprotects itself by spraying\npoisonous sweat from its pores.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00198" index="198">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Feared and loathed by many,\nit is believed to bring misfortune to\nall those who see it at night.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00199" index="199">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has incredible intellect and\nintuition. Whatever the situation,\nit remains calm and collected.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00200" index="200">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It likes playing mischievous tricks,\nsuch as screaming and wailing to\nstartle people at night. </language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00201" index="201">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their shapes look like hieroglyphs\non ancient tablets. It is said\nthat the two are somehow related.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00202" index="202">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It hates light and shock. If\nattacked, it inflates its body to\nbuild up its counterstrike.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00203" index="203">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its tail has a small brain of its\nown. Beware! If you get close, it\nmay react to your scent by biting.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00204" index="204">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It likes to make its shell thicker\nby adding layers of tree bark. The\nadditional weight doesn’t bother it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00205" index="205">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its entire body is shielded by a\nsteel-hard shell. What lurks inside\nthis shell is a total mystery.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00206" index="206">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When spotted, this Pokémon escapes\nbackward by furiously boring into\nthe ground with its tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00207" index="207">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flies straight at its target’s\nface, then clamps down on the\nstartled victim to inject poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00208" index="208">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body has been compressed deep\nunder the ground. As a result,\nit is even harder than a diamond.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00209" index="209">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Although it looks frightening, it\nis actually kind and affectionate.\nIt is very popular among women.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00210" index="210">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is actually timid and easily\nspooked. If attacked, it flails\nabout to fend off its attacker.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00211" index="211">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To fire its poison spikes, it must\ninflate its body by drinking over\n2.6 gallons of water all at once.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00212" index="212">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It swings its eye-patterned pincers\nup to scare its foes. This makes\nit look like it has three heads.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00213" index="213">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The berries it stores in its\nvase-like shell decompose and\nbecome a gooey liquid.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00214" index="214">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This powerful Pokémon thrusts\nits prized horn under its enemies’\nbellies, then lifts and throws them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00215" index="215">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its paws conceal sharp claws. If\nattacked, it suddenly extends the\nclaws and startles its enemy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00216" index="216">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it finds honey, its crescent mark\nglows. It always licks its paws\nbecause they’re soaked with honey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00217" index="217">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Although it is a good climber,\nit prefers to snap trees with its\nforelegs and eat fallen berries.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00218" index="218">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It never sleeps. It has to keep\nmoving because if it stopped, its\nmagma body would cool and harden.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00219" index="219">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The shell on its back is just skin\nthat has cooled and hardened. It\nbreaks easily with a slight touch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00220" index="220">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It rubs its snout on the ground to\nfind and dig up food. It sometimes\ndiscovers hot springs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00221" index="221">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because the long hair all over its\nbody obscures its sight, it just\nkeeps charging repeatedly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00222" index="222">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It continuously sheds and grows.\nThe tip of its head is prized as\na treasure because of its beauty.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00223" index="223">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has superb accuracy. The water\nit shoots out can strike moving\nprey from more than 300 feet away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00224" index="224">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It traps foes with the suction cups\non its tentacles, then smashes\nthem with its rock-hard head.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00225" index="225">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It carries food all day long.\nThere are tales about lost people\nwho were saved by its stored food.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00226" index="226">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it majestically swims, it doesn’t\ncare if REMORAID attach to it for\nscavenging its leftovers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00227" index="227">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its sturdy wings look heavy, but\nthey are actually hollow and light,\nallowing it to fly freely in the sky.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00228" index="228">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses different kinds of cries for\ncommunicating with others of its\nkind and for pursuing its prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00229" index="229">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If you are burned by the flames\nit shoots from its mouth,\nthe pain will never go away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00230" index="230">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that it usually hides in\nunderwater caves. It can create\nwhirlpools by yawning.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00231" index="231">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It swings its long snout around\nplayfully, but because it is so\nstrong, that can be dangerous.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00232" index="232">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has sharp, hard tusks and a\nrugged hide. Its tackle is strong\nenough to knock down a house.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00233" index="233">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This upgraded version of PORYGON\nis designed for space exploration.\nIt can’t fly, however.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00234" index="234">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The curved antlers subtly change\nthe flow of air to create a strange\nspace where reality is distorted.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00235" index="235">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A special fluid oozes from the tip\nof its tail. It paints the fluid\neverywhere to mark its territory.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00236" index="236">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is always bursting with energy.\nTo make itself stronger, it\nkeeps on fighting even if it loses.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00237" index="237">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If you are enchanted by its smooth,\ndance-like kicks, you may get a closer\nexperience with one than you’d like.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00238" index="238">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its lips are the most sensitive\npart of its body. It always uses\nits lips first to examine things.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00239" index="239">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It rotates its arms to generate\nelectricity, but it tires easily,\nso it only charges up a little bit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00240" index="240">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Each and every time it inhales\nand exhales, hot embers dribble\nfrom its mouth and nostrils.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00241" index="241">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its milk is packed with nutrition,\nmaking it the ultimate beverage\nfor the sick or weary.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00242" index="242">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Anyone who takes even one taste of\nBLISSEY’s egg becomes unfailingly\ncaring and pleasant to everyone.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00243" index="243">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The rain clouds it carries let it\nfire thunderbolts at will. They say\nthat it descended with lightning.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00244" index="244">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Volcanoes erupt when it barks.\nUnable to contain its sheer power,\nit races headlong around the land.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00245" index="245">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Said to be the embodiment of\nnorth winds, it can instantly\npurify filthy, murky water.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00246" index="246">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It feeds on soil. After it has eaten\na large mountain, it falls asleep\nso it can grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00247" index="247">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its shell is as hard as sheet rock,\nand it is also very strong. Its\nthrashing can topple a mountain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00248" index="248">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body can’t be harmed by any\nsort of attack, so it is very eager\nto make challenges against enemies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00249" index="249">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that it quietly spends its\ntime deep at the bottom of the sea\nbecause its powers are too strong.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00250" index="250">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Legends claim this Pokémon flies the\nworld’s skies continuously on its\nmagnificent, seven-colored wings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00251" index="251">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon wanders across time.\nGrass and trees flourish in the\nforests in which it has appeared.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00252" index="252">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Small hooks on the bottom of its\nfeet catch on walls and ceilings.\nThat is how it can hang from above.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00253" index="253">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It leaps from tree branch to tree\nbranch quite swiftly. It shows\nastounding agility.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00254" index="254">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It agilely leaps about the jungle\nand uses the sharp leaves on its\narms to strike its prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00255" index="255">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Inside its body is a place where it\nkeeps a small flame. Hug it! It will\nbe as warm as a hot-water bottle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00256" index="256">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">During a battle, the hot flame in\nits body increases. Its kicks have\noutstanding destructive power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00257" index="257">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can clear a 30-story building\nin a leap. Its fiery punches scorch\nits foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00258" index="258">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its power can crush boulders.\nIt rests by covering itself with mud\nat the bottom of a river.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00259" index="259">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Living on muddy ground that\nprovides poor footing has made\nits legs sturdy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00260" index="260">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its arms are hard as rock.\nWith one swing, it can\nbreak a boulder into pieces.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00261" index="261">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It chases its prey until the victim\nbecomes exhausted. However, it\nturns tail if the prey strikes back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00262" index="262">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It chases down prey in a pack of\naround ten. They defeat foes with\nperfectly coordinated teamwork.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00263" index="263">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gets interested in everything,\nwhich is why it zigs and zags.\nIt is good at finding items.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00264" index="264">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When running in a straight line, it\ncan easily top 60 miles an hour. It\nhas a tough time with curved roads.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00265" index="265">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives among the tall grass and in\nforests. It repels attacks by \nraising up the spikes on its rear.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00266" index="266">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Having wrapped silk around the\nbranches of a tree, it quiescently\nawaits evolution.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00267" index="267">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Vibrantly patterned wings are its\nprominent feature. It sucks sweet\nflower nectar with its long mouth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00268" index="268">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It endures attacks with patience,\nbecause the more pain before\nevolution, the sturdier it becomes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00269" index="269">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It scatters its fine dust all over\nwhen it is attacked. It is a\nnocturnal Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00270" index="270">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its leaf grew too large for it to\nlive on land. That is how it began\nto live floating in the water.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00271" index="271">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is nocturnal and becomes active\nat nightfall. It feeds on aquatic\nmosses that grow in the riverbed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00272" index="272">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it hears festive music, it begins\nmoving in rhythm in order to\namplify its power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00273" index="273">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attaches itself to a tree branch\nusing the top of its head. Strong\nwinds can sometimes make it fall.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00274" index="274">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives deep in forests. With the\nleaf on its head, it makes a flute\nwhose song makes listeners uneasy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00275" index="275">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives quietly in the deep forest.\nIt is said to create chilly winter\nwinds with the fans it holds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00276" index="276">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it gets cold, they migrate,\nflying over 180 miles a day.\nIt hunts for tasty prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00277" index="277">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It dives at a steep angle as soon\nas it spots its prey. It catches\nits prey with sharp claws.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00278" index="278">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It soars on updrafts without\nflapping its wings. It makes a nest\non sheer cliffs at the sea’s edge.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00279" index="279">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It protects its young in its beak.\nIt bobs on waves, resting on them\non days when the waters are calm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00280" index="280">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The horns on its head provide a\nstrong power that enables\nit to sense people’s emotions.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00281" index="281">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a psychic power that\nenables it to distort the space\naround it and see into the future.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00282" index="282">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It unleashes psychokinetic energy\nat full power when protecting a\nTrainer it has bonded closely with.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00283" index="283">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It secretes a thick, sweet-scented\nsyrup from the tip of its head.\nIt lives on weed-choked ponds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00284" index="284">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flaps its four wings to hover and\nfly freely in any direction--\nto and fro and sideways.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00285" index="285">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it senses danger, it scatters\nspores from the top of its head to\nprotect itself.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00286" index="286">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It scatters poisonous spores and\nthrows powerful punches while its\nfoe is hampered by inhaled spores.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00287" index="287">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The way SLAKOTH lolls around makes\nanyone who watches it feel like\ndoing the same.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00288" index="288">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its stress level rises if it\ncannot keep moving constantly.\nToo much stress makes it feel sick.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00289" index="289">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The world’s laziest Pokémon.\nIt moves to another spot when there’s\nno food left within its reach.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00290" index="290">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can sometimes live underground for\nmore than 10 years. It absorbs\nnutrients from the roots of trees.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00291" index="291">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its cry leaves a lasting headache\nif heard for too long. It moves so\nquickly that it is almost invisible.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00292" index="292">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A strange Pokémon--it flies without\nmoving its wings, has a hollow shell\nfor a body, and does not breathe.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00293" index="293">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it senses danger, it scares\nthe foe by crying out with the\nvolume of a jet-plane engine.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00294" index="294">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shouts loudly by inhaling air, and\nthen uses its well-developed\nstomach muscles to exhale.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00295" index="295">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its roar in battle shakes the\nground like a tremor--or like\nan earthquake has struck.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00296" index="296">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It toughens up by slamming into\nthick trees over and over. It gains\na sturdy body and dauntless spirit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00297" index="297">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves challenging others to\ntests of strength. It has the\npower to stop a train with a slap.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00298" index="298">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its tail is packed full of the\nnutrients it needs to grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00299" index="299">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If two of these meet, they cannot\nget too close because their noses\nrepel each other.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00300" index="300">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s adorable when it chases its own\ntail. It’s difficult to earn its trust.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00301" index="301">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It dislikes dirty places. It often\nsearches for a comfortable place\nin which to groom itself.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00302" index="302">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It dwells in the darkness of caves.\nIt uses its sharp claws to dig up\ngems to nourish itself.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00303" index="303">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It chomps with its gaping mouth.\nIts huge jaws are actually steel\nhorns that have been transformed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00304" index="304">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it evolves, it sheds the steel\ncarapace that covered its whole body\nand develops a new one.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00305" index="305">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves iron ore. Groups of them\nfight for territory by bashing one\nanother with their steel bodies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00306" index="306">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">You can tell its age by the length\nof its iron horns. It claims an\nentire mountain as its territory.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00307" index="307">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It meditates to heighten its inner\nenergy and to float in the air.\nIt eats one berry a day.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00308" index="308">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Through yoga training, it gained\nthe psychic power to predict\nits foe’s next move.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00309" index="309">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stores electricity in its fur. It\ngives off sparks from all over its\nbody in seasons when the air is dry.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00310" index="310">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its nest can be found where a\nthunderbolt hits. It is discharging\nelectricity from its mane.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00311" index="311">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It absorbs electricity from\ntelephone poles. It shorts out its\nbody to create crackling noises.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00312" index="312">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Exposure to electricity from MINUN\nand PLUSLE promotes blood\ncirculation and relaxes muscles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00313" index="313">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It emits light from its tail to\ncommunicate. It loves the\nsweet aroma given off by ILLUMISE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00314" index="314">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its fragrance attracts a swarm of\nVOLBEAT, so they draw over 200\npatterns in the night sky.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00315" index="315">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">ROSELIA that drink nutritionally\nrich springwater are said to reveal\nrare coloration when they bloom.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00316" index="316">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a small heart and brain. Its\nstomach comprises most of its body,\nwith enzymes to dissolve anything.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00317" index="317">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gulps anything that fits in its\nmouth. Its special enzymes can\ndissolve anything.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00318" index="318">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They form packs to attack boats\nand rip out their hulls to sink them.\nThey live in rivers in the jungle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00319" index="319">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can swim at speeds of 75 mph by\njetting seawater through its body.\nIt is the bandit of the sea.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00320" index="320">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It bounces playfully like a ball.\nThe more seawater it swallows,\nthe higher it bounces.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00321" index="321">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is the largest of all identified\nPokémon. They jump as a pack\nto herd their prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00322" index="322">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The flaming magma it stores in the\nhump on its back is the source of\nits tremendous power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00323" index="323">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in the crater of a volcano.\nIt is well known that the humps on\nits back erupt every 10 years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00324" index="324">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">You find abandoned coal mines full\nof them. They dig tirelessly in\nsearch of coal.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00325" index="325">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It bounces around on its tail to\nkeep its heart pumping. It carries\na pearl from CLAMPERL on its head.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00326" index="326">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can perform odd dance steps to\ninfluence foes. Its style of dancing\nbecame hugely popular overseas.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00327" index="327">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The chances of two SPINDA having\nidentical spot patterns is less\nthan one in four billion.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00328" index="328">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its nest is a sloped, bowl-like pit\nin the desert. Once something has\nfallen in, there is no escape.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00329" index="329">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It vibrates its wings vigorously,\ncreating ultrasonic waves that\ncause serious headaches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00330" index="330">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is nicknamed “The Desert\nSpirit” because the flapping of its\nwings sounds like a woman singing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00331" index="331">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in arid locations. Its\nyellow flowers bloom once a year.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00332" index="332">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Packs of them follow travelers\nthrough the desert until\nthe travelers can no longer move.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00333" index="333">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its wings bring cottony clouds to\nmind. It grooms with springwater\nand loves to sit on heads.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00334" index="334">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flies gracefully through the\nsky. Its melodic humming makes\nyou feel like you’re in a dream.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00335" index="335">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its fur would all stand on end if\nit smelled a SEVIPER nearby.\nIts sharp claws tear up its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00336" index="336">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In battle, it uses its bladed tail to\ncounter any ZANGOOSE. It secretes\na deadly venom in its tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00337" index="337">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It was discovered at the site of a\nmeteor strike 40 years ago. Its\nstare can lull its foes to sleep.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00338" index="338">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it rotates itself, it gives off\nlight similar to the sun, thus\nblinding its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00339" index="339">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">BARBOACH uses its whiskers to\ntaste things just as a person uses\nhis or her tongue to taste things.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00340" index="340">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It claims a large swamp to itself.\nIf a foe comes near it, it sets off\ntremors by thrashing around.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00341" index="341">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It was originally a Pokémon from\nafar that escaped to the wild. It\ncan adapt to the dirtiest river.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00342" index="342">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A brutish Pokémon that loves to\nbattle. It will crash itself into any\nfoe that approaches its nest.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00343" index="343">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It moves while spinning around on\nits single foot. Some BALTOY have\nbeen seen spinning on their heads.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00344" index="344">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that it originates from clay\ndolls made by an ancient civilization.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00345" index="345">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It disguises its tentacles as\nflowers to attract and catch prey.\nIt became extinct in ancient times.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00346" index="346">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in warm seas. Its heavy\nbody weighs it down so it won’t\nget washed away in rough weather.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00347" index="347">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An ancestral Pokémon that lived in\nthe ocean. Over time, its eight feet\ntransformed into wings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00348" index="348">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its enormous, retractable claws\ncan cut through most anything. Its\nentire body is clad in sturdy plates.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00349" index="349">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is the shabbiest Pokémon of all.\nIt forms in schools and lives at the\nbottom of rivers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00350" index="350">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s said that a glimpse of a\nMILOTIC and its beauty will calm any\nhostile emotions you’re feeling.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00351" index="351">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon can change its cells,\ntaking different forms based on\nthe temperature and humidity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00352" index="352">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It changes its shading to match its\nsurroundings so it can sneak up on prey.\nOnly its belly patterns stay fixed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00353" index="353">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses its horn to feed on envy\nand malice, or so it’s said.\nIt’s very active at night.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00354" index="354">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon developed from an\nabandoned doll that amassed a\ngrudge. It is seen in dark alleys.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00355" index="355">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it finds bad children who won’t\nlisten to their parents, it will\nspirit them away--or so it’s said.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00356" index="356">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Anyone who dares peer into its body\nto see its spectral ball of fire\nwill have their spirit stolen away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00357" index="357">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The bunch of fruit around its neck\nripens twice a year and is delicious.\nIt’s a highly favored tropical snack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00358" index="358">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses the sucker on its head to\nhang from a tree or from eaves. It\ncan produce seven different tones.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00359" index="359">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has the ability to foretell\nnatural disasters. Its life span is\nover a hundred years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00360" index="360">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It tends to move in a pack.\nIndividuals squash against one\nanother to toughen their spirits.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00361" index="361">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s said that if they are seen at\nmidnight, they’ll cause heavy snow.\nThey eat snow and ice to survive.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00362" index="362">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can instantly freeze moisture in\nthe atmosphere. It uses this power\nto freeze its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00363" index="363">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It crosses the oceans by rolling itself\non drifting ice. Fluffy fur keeps it warm\nwhen the temperature is below freezing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00364" index="364">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a very sensitive nose.\nIt touches new things with its nose\nto examine them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00365" index="365">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shatters drift ice with its\nstrong tusks. Its thick layer of\nblubber repels enemy attacks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00366" index="366">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it evolves, it makes a\nmysterious pearl that amplifies\npsychic powers when it’s held.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00367" index="367">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives deep in the pitch-dark sea.\nIt attracts prey by moving its tail\nin mimicry of a small animal.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00368" index="368">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its pink body becomes more vivid\nwith the rise of water\ntemperatures in the springtime.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00369" index="369">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Discovered by chance during\ndeep-sea explorations, it has not\nchanged since ancient times.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00370" index="370">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its heart-shaped body makes it\npopular. In some places, you would\ngive a LUVDISC to someone you love.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00371" index="371">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its well-developed neck muscles\nand ironlike head can smash\nboulders into pieces.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00372" index="372">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It surrounds its body in an\niron-hard shell to accumulate\nenough power to evolve.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00373" index="373">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s uncontrollable if enraged.\nIt flies around spouting flames and\nscorching fields and mountains.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00374" index="374">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The magnetic force generated by\nits body repels the ground’s\nnatural magnetism, letting it float. </language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00375" index="375">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When two BELDUM fuse together, a\nmagnetic nervous system places\ntheir brains in union.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00376" index="376">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It folds its four legs when flying.\nIts four brains are said to be\nsuperior to a supercomputer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00377" index="377">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The same rocks that form its body\nhave been found in ground layers\naround the world.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00378" index="378">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to have slept in a glacier\nfor thousands of years. Its body\ncan’t be melted, even by magma.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00379" index="379">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is said to be harder than\nany kind of metal. A study has\nrevealed that its body is hollow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00380" index="380">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It communicates using telepathy.\nIts body is covered in down that\nrefracts light to make it invisible.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00381" index="381">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It understands human speech and is\nhighly intelligent. It is a tender\nPokémon that dislikes fighting.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00382" index="382">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mythical Pokémon said to have\nswelled the seas with rain and tidal\nwaves. It battled with GROUDON.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00383" index="383">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Said to have expanded the lands by\nevaporating water with raging heat.\nIt battled titanically with KYOGRE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00384" index="384">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flies in the ozone layer, way up\nhigh in the sky. Until recently,\nno one had ever seen it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00385" index="385">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Generations have believed that any\nwish written on a note on its head\nwill come true when it awakens.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00386" index="386">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">DNA from a space virus mutated and\nbecame a Pokémon. It appears\nwhere auroras are seen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00387" index="387">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Photosynthesis occurs across its\nbody under the sun. The shell on\nits back is actually hardened soil.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00388" index="388">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A GROTLE that lives in the forest\nis said to have its own secret\nspringwater.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00389" index="389">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ancient people imagined that\nbeneath the ground, a gigantic\nTORTERRA dwelled.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00390" index="390">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The gas made in its belly burns from\nits rear end. The fire burns weakly\nwhen it feels sick.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00391" index="391">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A bigger fire on its tail and a\nbrighter blue pattern on its face\nmeans its rank in its pack is higher.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00392" index="392">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It tosses its enemies around with\nagility. It uses all its limbs to\nfight in its own unique style.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00393" index="393">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It doesn’t like to be taken care\nof. It’s difficult to bond with since\nit won’t listen to its Trainer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00394" index="394">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives a solitary life. Its wings\ndeliver wicked blows that can\nsnap even the thickest of trees.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00395" index="395">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It avoids unnecessary disputes,\nbut it will decimate anything that\nthreatens its pride.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00396" index="396">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They flock around mountains and\nfields, chasing after bug Pokémon.\nTheir singing is noisy and annoying.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00397" index="397">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They maintain huge flocks, although\nfierce scuffles break out between\nvarious flocks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00398" index="398">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When STARAVIA evolve into\nSTARAPTOR, they leave the flock to\nlive alone. They have sturdy wings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00399" index="399">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in groups by the water. \nIt chews up boulders and trees\naround its nest with its incisors.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00400" index="400">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It busily makes its nest with\nstacks of branches and roots it\nhas cut up with its sharp incisors.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00401" index="401">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its antennae hit each other,\nit sounds like the music of\na xylophone.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00402" index="402">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By allowing its cry to resonate in\nthe hollow of its belly, it produces\na captivating sound.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00403" index="403">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The extension and contraction of\nits muscles generates electricity.\nIts fur glows when it’s in trouble.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00404" index="404">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By gathering their tails together,\nthey collectively generate powerful\nelectricity from their claws. </language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00405" index="405">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">LUXRAY’s ability to see through\nobjects comes in handy when it’s\nscouting for danger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00406" index="406">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it feels the sun’s warm touch,\nit opens its bud to release pollen.\nIt lives alongside clear pools.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00407" index="407">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its sweet aroma attracts prey.\nThen it spews poison. The more\ntoxic it is, the sweeter its aroma.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00408" index="408">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">CRANIDOS toughen up their already\nrock-hard heads by headbutting\none another.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00409" index="409">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its skull withstands impacts of any\nmagnitude. As a result, its brain\nnever gets the chance to grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00410" index="410">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It was generated from a fossil dug out\nof a layer of clay that was older than\nanyone knows. It has a sturdy face.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00411" index="411">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When attacked, they form a wall.\nTheir rock-hard faces serve to\nprotect them from the attacks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00412" index="412">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It covers itself with a cloak to\nshelter from the cold. When it’s\nhot, its cloak is thinner.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00413" index="413">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that a WORMADAM that\nevolves on a cold day will have a\nthicker cloak.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00414" index="414">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flutters around at night and\nsteals honey from the COMBEE hive.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00415" index="415">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">At night, COMBEE sleep in a group of\nabout a thousand, packed closely\ntogether in a lump.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00416" index="416">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It raises grubs in the holes in its\nbody. It secretes pheromones to\ncontrol COMBEE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00417" index="417">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s one of the kinds of Pokémon \nwith electric cheek pouches.\nIt shoots charges from its tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00418" index="418">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It inflates its flotation sac,\nkeeping its face above water in\norder to watch for prey movement.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00419" index="419">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With its flotation sac inflated, it\ncan carry people on its back. It\ndeflates the sac before it dives.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00420" index="420">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It evolves by sucking the energy\nout of the small ball where it had\nbeen storing nutrients.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00421" index="421">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">During times of strong sunlight,\nits bud blooms, its petals open\nfully, and it becomes very active.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00422" index="422">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its shape and coloration vary,\ndepending on its habitat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00423" index="423">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its natural enemy attacks,\nit oozes purple fluid and escapes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00424" index="424">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They live on large trees. They are\nsaid to communicate by connecting\ntheir tails to those of others.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00425" index="425">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is whispered that any child who\nmistakes DRIFLOON for a balloon and\nholds on to it could wind up missing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00426" index="426">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can generate and release gas\nwithin its body. That’s how it can\ncontrol the altitude of its drift.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00427" index="427">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">You can tell how it feels by the way\nit rolls its ears. When it’s scared,\nboth ears are rolled up.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00428" index="428">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sheds its fur twice a year.\nIts winter fur is soft and fluffy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00429" index="429">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its cries sound like incantations\nto torment the foe. It appears\nwhere you least expect it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00430" index="430">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is merciless by nature. It is said\nthat it never forgives the mistakes\nof its MURKROW followers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00431" index="431">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it’s happy, GLAMEOW\ndemonstrates beautiful movements\nof its tail, like a dancing ribbon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00432" index="432">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It would claim another Pokémon’s\nnest as its own if it finds a nest\nsufficiently comfortable.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00433" index="433">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It emits high-frequency cries that \npeople can’t hear. Once it starts,\nit can cry for an awfully long time. </language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00434" index="434">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The foul fluid from its rear is so\nrevolting that it can make people feel\nqueasy up to a mile and a quarter away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00435" index="435">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attacks by spraying a repugnant\nfluid from its tail, but the stench\ndulls after a few squirts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00436" index="436">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ancient people believed that the\npattern on BRONZOR’s back\ncontained a mysterious power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00437" index="437">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ancient people believed that\npetitioning BRONZONG for rain\nwas the way to make crops grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00438" index="438">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In order to adjust the level of fluids in\nits body, it exudes water from its eyes.\nThis makes it appear to be crying.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00439" index="439">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In an attempt to confuse its enemy,\nit mimics the enemy’s movements. Then\nit wastes no time in making itself scarce!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00440" index="440">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It carefully carries a round, white rock\nthat it thinks is an egg. It’s bothered\nby how curly its hair looks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00441" index="441">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It mimics the cries of other Pokémon to\ntrick them into thinking it’s one of them.\nThis way they won’t attack it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00442" index="442">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It was formed by uniting 108 spirits.\nIt has been bound to the Odd Keystone\nto keep it from doing any mischief.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00443" index="443">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It nests in horizontal holes warmed by\ngeothermal heat. Foes who get too close\ncan expect to be pounced on and bitten.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00444" index="444">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it digs to expand its nest, it\nhabitually digs up gems that it\nthen hoards in its nest.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00445" index="445">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is covered in fine scales that\nreduce drag, enabling it to fly at\nhigh speeds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00446" index="446">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It conceals food under the long fur on\nits body. It carts around this food\nstash and swallows it without chewing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00447" index="447">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They communicate with one another\nusing their auras. They are able to run\nall through the night.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00448" index="448">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s said that no foe can remain invisible\nto LUCARIO, since it can detect auras.\nEven foes it could not otherwise see.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00449" index="449">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shrouds itself in sand to ward off\ngerms. It travels easily through the\nsands of the desert.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00450" index="450">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It brandishes its gaping mouth in a\ndisplay of fearsome strength. It raises\nvast quantities of sand while attacking.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00451" index="451">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It burrows under the sand to lie in\nwait for prey. Its tail claws can inject\nits prey with a savage poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00452" index="452">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attacks people and Pokémon that\ncross the desert. This has only\nfurthered its bad reputation.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00453" index="453">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Fluid squeezed from its finger, albeit\npoisonous, is a significant ingredient in\nremedies for lower-back pain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00454" index="454">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Swaying and dodging the attacks of its\nfoes, it weaves its flexible body in close,\nthen lunges out with its poisonous claws.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00455" index="455">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It walks around on its tentacles in\nsearch of a tree branch where it\ncan dangle down and ambush prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00456" index="456">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Swimming and fluttering its two tail fins,\nit looks like a BEAUTIFLY. At night, the\npatterns on its tail fins softly shine.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00457" index="457">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">LUMINEON swimming in the darkness\nof the deep sea look like stars shining\nin the night sky.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00458" index="458">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it swims close to the surface of the\nocean, people aboard ships are able to\nobserve the pattern on its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00459" index="459">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">During cold seasons, it migrates to the\nmountain’s lower reaches. It returns to\nthe snow-covered summit in the spring.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00460" index="460">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives a quiet life on mountains that\nare perpetually covered in snow.\nIt hides itself by whipping up blizzards.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00461" index="461">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in snowy regions. It carves\npatterns in trees with its claws as\na signal to others.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00462" index="462">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Exposure to a special magnetic field\nchanged MAGNETON’s molecular\nstructure, turning it into MAGNEZONE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00463" index="463">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its saliva can decompose anything.\nIt wraps its long tongue around things\nto coat them with its sticky saliva.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00464" index="464">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">From holes in its palms, it fires out\nGEODUDE. Its carapace \ncan withstand volcanic eruptions.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00465" index="465">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it remains still, it appears to be a\nlarge shrub. Unsuspecting prey that\nwander near get ensnared by its vines.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00466" index="466">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As its electric charge amplifies,\nblue sparks begin to crackle between\nits horns.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00467" index="467">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It blasts fireballs of over\n3,600 degrees Fahrenheit out of its\narms. Its breath also sears and sizzles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00468" index="468">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As everyone knows, it visits peaceful\nregions, bringing them gifts of kindness\nand sweet blessings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00469" index="469">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This six-legged Pokémon is easily capable\nof transporting an adult in flight. The\nwings on its tail help it stay balanced.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00470" index="470">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When you see LEAFEON asleep in a patch\nof sunshine, you’ll know it is using\nphotosynthesis to produce clean air.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00471" index="471">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It causes small ice crystals to form by\nlowering the temperature of the\nsurrounding atmosphere.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00472" index="472">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its flight is soundless. It uses its\nlengthy tail to carry off its prey...\nThen its elongated fangs do the rest.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00473" index="473">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A frozen MAMOSWINE was dug from ice\ndating back 10,000 years. This Pokémon\nhas been around a long, long, long time.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00474" index="474">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its programming was modified to enable\nit to travel through alien dimensions.\nSeems there might have been an error...</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00475" index="475">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because it can sense what its foe\nis thinking, its attacks burst out\nfirst, fast, and fierce.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00476" index="476">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It controls three units called Mini-Noses\nusing magnetic force. With them, it can\nattack the foe from three directions.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00477" index="477">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This feared Pokémon is said to travel to\nworlds unknown. Some even believe that\nit takes lost spirits along with it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00478" index="478">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Legends in snowy regions say that\na woman who was lost on an icy\nmountain was reborn as FROSLASS.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00479" index="479">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Research continues on this Pokémon,\nwhich could be the power source of a\nunique motor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00480" index="480">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">According to some sources, this Pokémon\nprovided people with the intelligence\nnecessary to solve various problems.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00481" index="481">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon is said to have endowed\nthe human heart with emotions, such as\nsorrow and joy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00482" index="482">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon is said to have endowed\nhumans with the determination needed\nto face any of life’s difficulties.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00483" index="483">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon completely controls the\nflow of time. It uses its power to travel\nat will through the past and future.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00484" index="484">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its total control over the boundaries\nof space enable it to transport itself to\nfaraway places or even other dimensions.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00485" index="485">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Boiling blood, like magma, circulates\nthrough its body. It makes its dwelling\nplace in volcanic caves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00486" index="486">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is believed to have shaped\nREGIROCK, REGICE, and REGISTEEL\nout of clay, ice, and magma.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00487" index="487">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon is said to live in a world on\nthe reverse side of ours, where common\nknowledge is distorted and strange.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00488" index="488">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Those who sleep holding CRESSELIA’s\nfeather are assured of joyful dreams. It\nis said to represent the crescent moon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00489" index="489">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the water warms, they inflate the\nflotation sac on their heads and drift\nlanguidly on the sea in packs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00490" index="490">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It starts its life with a wondrous power\nthat permits it to bond with any kind\nof Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00491" index="491">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It chases people and Pokémon from its\nterritory by causing them to experience\ndeep, nightmarish slumbers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00492" index="492">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The blooming of Gracidea flowers confers\nthe power of flight upon it. Feelings \nof gratitude are the message it delivers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_00493" index="493">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">According to the legends of Sinnoh, this\nPokémon emerged from an egg and\nshaped all there is in this world.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_unused_494" index="494">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English"></language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_unused_495" index="495">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English"></language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_496" index="496">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">DNA from a space virus mutated and\nbecame a Pokémon. It appears\nwhere auroras are seen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_497" index="497">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">DNA from a space virus mutated and\nbecame a Pokémon. It appears\nwhere auroras are seen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_498" index="498">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">DNA from a space virus mutated and\nbecame a Pokémon. It appears\nwhere auroras are seen.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_499" index="499">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that a WORMADAM that\nevolves on a cold day will have a\nthicker cloak.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_500" index="500">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that a WORMADAM that\nevolves on a cold day will have a\nthicker cloak.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_501" index="501">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon is said to live in a world on\nthe reverse side of ours, where common\nknowledge is distorted and strange.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_502" index="502">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The blooming of Gracidea flowers confers\nthe power of flight upon it. Feelings \nof gratitude are the message it delivers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_503" index="503">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Research continues on this Pokémon,\nwhich could be the power source of a\nunique motor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_504" index="504">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Research continues on this Pokémon,\nwhich could be the power source of a\nunique motor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_505" index="505">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Research continues on this Pokémon,\nwhich could be the power source of a\nunique motor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_506" index="506">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Research continues on this Pokémon,\nwhich could be the power source of a\nunique motor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_form_507" index="507">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Research continues on this Pokémon,\nwhich could be the power source of a\nunique motor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_lillipup" index="508">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Though it is a very brave Pokémon,\nit’s also smart enough to check\nits foe’s strength and avoid battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_herdier" index="509">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very loyal Pokémon helps Trainers,\nand it also takes care of other Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_stoutland" index="510">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Being wrapped in its long fur is so\ncomfortable that a person would be fine\neven overnight on a wintry mountain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_purrloin" index="511">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their cute act is a ruse. They trick\npeople and steal their valuables\njust to see the looks on their faces.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_liepard" index="512">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their beautiful form comes from\nthe muscles they have developed.\nThey run silently in the night.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tympole" index="513">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By vibrating its cheeks, it emits\nsound waves imperceptible to humans\nand warns others of danger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_palpitoad" index="514">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in the water and on land.\nIt uses its long, sticky tongue\nto immobilize its opponents.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_seismitoad" index="515">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By putting power into its bumps,\nit creates vibrations and\nincreases the power of its punches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sewaddle" index="516">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Since this Pokémon makes its own clothes\nout of leaves, it is a popular mascot for\nfashion designers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_swadloon" index="517">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Preferring dark, damp places,\nit spends the entire day eating\nfallen leaves that lie around it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_leavanny" index="518">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Upon finding a small Pokémon, it weaves\nclothing for it from leaves by using\nthe sticky silk secreted from its mouth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_yamask" index="519">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon arose from the\nspirits of people interred in graves.\nEach retains memories of its former life.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cofagrigus" index="520">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Grave robbers who mistake them\nfor real coffins and get too close\nend up trapped inside their bodies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_trubbish" index="521">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Wanting more garbage, they\nfollow people who litter.\nThey always belch poison gas.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_garbodor" index="522">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Consuming garbage makes\nnew kinds of poison gases\nand liquids inside their bodies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_emolga" index="523">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It glides on its outstretched membrane\nwhile shocking foes with the electricity\nstored in the pouches on its cheeks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_karrablast" index="524">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For some reason they evolve when they\nreceive electrical energy while they\nare attacking Shelmet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_escavalier" index="525">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Wearing the shell covering they stole\nfrom Shelmet, they defend themselves\nand attack with two lances.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_foongus" index="526">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lures Pokémon with its pattern\nthat looks just like a Poké Ball\nthen releases poison spores.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_amoonguss" index="527">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It moves the caps on both arms\nand does a dance to lure prey.\nIt prefers damp places.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_joltik" index="528">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Since it can’t generate its own electricity,\nit sticks onto large-bodied Pokémon and\nabsorbs static electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_galvantula" index="529">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It creates barriers from\nelectrified silk that stun foes.\nThis works as a weapon as well as a defense.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_ferroseed" index="530">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It absorbs the iron it finds in\nthe rock while clinging to the ceiling.\nIt shoots spikes when in danger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_ferrothorn" index="531">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By swinging around its three\nspiky feelers and shooting spikes,\nit can obliterate an opponent.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_klink" index="532">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Two bodies comprise a fixed pair.\nThey spin around each\nother to generate energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_klang" index="533">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A minigear and big gear comprise its body.\nIf the minigear it launches at\na foe doesn’t return, it will die.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_klinklang" index="534">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The minigear spins at high speed.\nThen the energy from the red core charges\nthe minigear to make it ready to fire.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_elgyem" index="535">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Rumors of its origin are\nlinked to a UFO crash site\nin the desert 50 years ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_beheeyem" index="536">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Apparently, it communicates by\nflashing its three fingers, but\nthose patterns haven’t been decoded.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_litwick" index="537">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its flame is usually out, but it\nstarts shining when Litwick absorbs\nlife-force from people or Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_lampent" index="538">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The spirits it absorbs fuel its baleful fire.\nIt hangs around hospitals\nwaiting for people to pass on.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_chandelure" index="539">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The spirits burned up in its\nominous flame lose their way\nand wander this world forever.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_shelmet" index="540">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it and Karrablast are together, and\nboth receive electrical stimulation,\nthey both evolve.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_accelgor" index="541">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its body dries out, it weakens.\nSo it wraps a membrane around itself\nfor protection while it spits poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_bouffalant" index="542">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They are known to charge so wildly that\nif a train were to enter their territory,\nthey would send it flying.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_bunnelby" index="543">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They use their large ears to dig\nburrows. They will dig the whole night\nthrough.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_diggersby" index="544">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As powerful as an excavator, its ears\ncan reduce dense bedrock to rubble.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_fletchling" index="545">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it’s excited, its temperature can\ndouble, spiking hormone production in\nits body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_fletchinder" index="546">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its speed right after takeoff already\nputs it in the top speed class of all\nbird Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_talonflame" index="547">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When attacking prey, it can reach\nspeeds of up to 310 mph. It finishes its\nprey off with a colossal kick.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_litleo" index="548">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The stronger the opponent it faces, the\nmore heat and power flow through its\nbody.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pyroar" index="549">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The male with the largest mane of fire\nis the leader of the pride.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_espurr" index="550">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The organ that emits its intense\npsychic power is sheltered by its ears\nto keep power from leaking out.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_meowstic" index="551">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When in danger, it raises its ears and\nreleases enough psychic power to grind\na 10-ton truck to dust.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sylveon" index="552">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sends a soothing aura from its\nribbonlike feelers to calm fights.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dedenne" index="553">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its upper whiskers are sensors that\nsurvey its surroundings. Its lower\nwhiskers shoot electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_phantump" index="554">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is created when a spirit possesses\nrotten tree stumps. It prefers to live\nin abandoned forests.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_trevenant" index="555">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can control trees at will. It will\ntrap people who harm the forest, so they\ncan never leave.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pumpkaboo" index="556">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said to carry wandering spirits\nto the place where they belong so they\ncan move on.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gourgeist" index="557">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It enwraps its prey in its hairlike\narms. It sings joyfully as it observes\nthe suffering of its prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_noibat" index="558">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They live in pitch black caves. Their\nenormous ears can emit ultrasonic waves\nof 200,000 hertz.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_noivern" index="559">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This hot-blooded Pokémon attacks\nanything it sees with ultrasonic waves\nthat can crush boulders.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_applin" index="560">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As soon as it’s born, it burrows into\nan apple. the flavor of the apple is\nwhat determines its evolution.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_flapple" index="561">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It ate a sour apple, which induced its\nevolution. It stores an acid capable of\ncausing chemical burns in its cheeks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_appletun" index="562">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It ate a sweet apple, which induced\nits evolution. Back in the day, children\nused to have it as a snack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sizzlipede" index="563">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stores flammable gas in its body\nand uses it to generate heat. It then\ncoils around its prey and cooks it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_centiskorch" index="564">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This excessively hostile Pokémon has\nlarge and very sharp fangs in addition\nto its dangerous burning body. </language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_wyrdeer" index="565">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The fur shed from its beard retains\nheat well and is a highly useful\nmaterial for winter clothing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_kleavor" index="566">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Parts of its body turned to stone when\nit evolved thanks to an extremely rare\nore found in volcanic areas.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_ursaluna" index="567">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">I believe it was Hisui’s swampy terrain that gave Ursaluna its\nburly physique and newfound capacity to manipulate peat\nat will.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_annihilape" index="568">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its anger rose beyond a critical\npoint, this Pokémon gained power that is\nunfettered by the limits of its physical body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_farigiraf" index="569">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The hardened head from the tail protects\nthe head of the main body as Farigiraf whips\nits long neck around to headbutt enemies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dudunsparce" index="570">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It drives enemies out of its nest by sucking\nin enough air to fill its long, narrow lungs,\nthen releasing the air in an intense blast.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dipplin" index="571">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Dipplin is two creatures in one Pokémon.\nIts evolution was triggered by a special\napple grown only in one place.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_hydrapple" index="572">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These capricious syrpents have banded\ntogether. On the rare occasion that their\nmoods align, their true power is unleashed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_slowpoke_galarian" index="573">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English"></language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_slowbro_galarian" index="574">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English"></language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_victini" index="575">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it shares the infinite energy\nit creates, that being’s entire body\nwill be overflowing with power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_snivy" index="576">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Being exposed to sunlight\nmakes its movements swifter.\nIt uses vines more adeptly than its hands.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_servine" index="577">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it gets dirty, its leaves\ncan’t be used in photosynthesis,\nso it always keeps itself clean.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_serperior" index="578">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It only gives its all against\nstrong opponents who are not fazed\nby the glare from Serperior’s noble eyes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tepig" index="579">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves to eat roasted berries,\nbut sometimes it gets too excited\nand burns them to a crisp.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pignite" index="580">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The more it eats, the more fuel it has\nto make the fire in its stomach stronger.\nThis fills it with even more power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_emboar" index="581">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A flaring beard of fire is\nproof that it is fired up.\nIt is adept at using many different moves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_oshawott" index="582">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The scalchop on its stomach isn’t\njust used for battle--it can be used\nto break open hard berries as well.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dewott" index="583">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As a result of strict training,\neach Dewott learns different\nforms for using the scalchops.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_samurott" index="584">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In the time it takes a foe to blink,\nit can draw and sheathe the seamitars\nattached to its front legs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_patrat" index="585">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Extremely cautious, one of them\nwill always be on the lookout, but it\nwon’t notice a foe coming from behind.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_watchog" index="586">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using luminescent matter,\nit makes its eyes and body glow\nand stuns attacking opponents.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pansage" index="587">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s good at finding berries\nand gathers them from all over.\nIt’s kind enough to share them with friends.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_simisage" index="588">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It strikes its enemies\nwith a thorn-covered tail.\nThe leaf on its head is bitter.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pansear" index="589">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Very intelligent, it roasts\nberries before eating them.\nIt likes to help people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_simisear" index="590">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it gets excited, embers rise\nfrom its head and tail and it gets hot.\nFor some reason, it loves sweets.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_panpour" index="591">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The water stored inside the tuft\non its head is full of nutrients.\nIt waters plants with it using its tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_simipour" index="592">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It prefers places with clean water.\nWhen its tuft runs low, it replenishes\nit by siphoning up water with its tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_munna" index="593">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon appears before people and\nPokémon who are having nightmares and\neats those dreams.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_musharna" index="594">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The dream mist coming from its forehead\nchanges into many different colors\ndepending on the dream that was eaten.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pidove" index="595">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very forgetful Pokémon will\nwait for a new order from its Trainer\neven though it already has one.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tranquill" index="596">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">No matter where in the world it goes,\nit knows where its nest is, so it never\ngets separated from its Trainer.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_unfezant" index="597">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Males swing the plumage on\ntheir heads to threaten others,\nbut females are better at flying.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_blitzle" index="598">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its mane shines when it discharges\nelectricity. They use the frequency and\nrhythm of these flashes to communicate.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_zebstrika" index="599">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When this ill-tempered Pokémon\nruns wild, it shoots lightning\nfrom its mane in all directions.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_roggenrola" index="600">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The hexagonal-shaped hole is its ear.\nIt has a tendency to walk in the\ndirection the sound is coming from.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_boldore" index="601">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it is healthy, its core sticks out.\nAlways facing the same way, it swiftly\nmoves front to back and left to right.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gigalith" index="602">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The solar rays it absorbs are\nprocessed in its energy core\nand fired as a ball of light.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_woobat" index="603">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The heart-shaped mark left on a body\nafter a Woobat has been attached\nto it is said to bring good fortune.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_swoobat" index="604">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It shakes its tail vigorously when it\nemits ultrasonic waves strong enough\nto reduce concrete to rubble.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_drilbur" index="605">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By spinning its body, it can dig\nstraight through the ground\nat a speed of 30 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_excadrill" index="606">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Forming a drill with its steel claws\nand head, it can bore through a steel\nplate, no matter how thick it is.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_audino" index="607">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using the feelers on its ears,\nit can tell how someone is feeling\nor when an egg might hatch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_timburr" index="608">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Always carrying squared logs,\nthey help out with construction.\nAs they grow, they carry bigger logs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gurdurr" index="609">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With strengthened bodies,\nthey skillfully wield steel\nbeams to take down buildings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_conkeldurr" index="610">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Rather than rely on force,\nthey master moves that utilize the\ncentrifugal force of spinning concrete.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_throh" index="611">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it encounters a foe bigger\nthan itself, it wants to throw it.\nIt changes belts as it gets stronger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sawk" index="612">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Desiring the strongest karate chop,\nthey seclude themselves in mountains\nand train without sleeping.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_venipede" index="613">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using the feelers on its head and tail,\nit picks up vibrations in the air to\ndetermine its prey’s location and state.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_whirlipede" index="614">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Storing energy for evolution, it sits.\nBut, when predators approach, it moves\nto stab them with poison spikes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_scolipede" index="615">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It clasps its prey with the claws\non its neck until it stops moving.\nThen it finishes it off with deadly poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cottonee" index="616">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Perhaps because they feel more at ease\nin a group, they stick to others they find.\nThey end up looking like a cloud.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_whimsicott" index="617">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They appear along with whirlwinds.\nThey pull pranks, such as moving furniture\nand leaving balls of cotton in homes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_petilil" index="618">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The leaves on its head grow right back\neven if they fall out. These bitter leaves\nrefresh those who eat them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_lilligant" index="619">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The fragrance of the garland\non its head has a relaxing effect,\nbut taking care of it is very difficult.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_basculin" index="620">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Red- and blue-striped Basculin are\nvery violent and always fighting.\nThey are also remarkably tasty.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sandile" index="621">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They live hidden under hot desert sands\nin order to keep their body temperature\nfrom dropping.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_krokorok" index="622">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Protected by thin membranes, their\neyes can see even in the dead of night.\nThey live in groups of a few individuals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_krookodile" index="623">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Very violent Pokémon, they try\nto clamp down on anything that\nmoves in front of their eyes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_darumaka" index="624">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it sleeps, it pulls its limbs\ninto its body and its internal fire\ngoes down to 1,100 degrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_darmanitan" index="625">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its internal fire burns at 2,500 degrees\nFahrenheit, making enough power that it\ncan destroy a dump truck with one punch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_maractus" index="626">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it moves rhythmically, it\nmakes a sound similar to maracas,\nmaking the surprised Pokémon flee.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dwebble" index="627">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it finds a stone of a suitable size,\nit secretes a liquid from its mouth\nto open up a hole to crawl into.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_crustle" index="628">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its boulder is broken in\nbattles for territory, it feels\nunsure and begins to weaken.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_scraggy" index="629">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Proud of its sturdy skull, it\nsuddenly headbutts everything,\nbut its weight makes it unstable, too.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_scrafty" index="630">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It pulls up its shed skin to protect\nitself while it kicks. The bigger\nthe crest, the more respected it is.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sigilyph" index="631">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The guardians of an ancient city,\nthey always fly the same route\nwhile keeping watch for invaders.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tirtouga" index="632">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon was restored from a fossil.\nIt swam skillfully and dove\nto depths beyond half a mile.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_carracosta" index="633">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It could knock out a foe with a slap from\none of its developed front appendages\nand chew it up, shell or bones and all.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_archen" index="634">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It was revived from an ancient fossil.\nNot able to fly, it lived in treetops\nand hopped from one branch to another.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_archeops" index="635">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It runs better than it flies.\nIt takes off into the sky by\nrunning at a speed of 25 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_zorua" index="636">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It changes so it looks just like its foe,\ntricks it, and then uses that opportunity\nto flee.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_zoroark" index="637">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Stories say those who tried to catch\nZoroark were trapped in an illusion\nand punished.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_minccino" index="638">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Minccino greet each other\nby grooming one another\nthoroughly with their tails.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cinccino" index="639">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Cinccino’s body is coated in a\nspecial oil that helps it deflect\nattacks, such as punches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gothita" index="640">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stares intently at everything.\nIt can become so obsessed with watching\nthat it doesn’t notice attacks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gothorita" index="641">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">According to many old tales, it creates\nfriends for itself by controlling sleeping\nchildren on starry nights.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gothitelle" index="642">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can see the future from the movement\nof the stars. When it learns its Trainer’s\nlife span, it cries in sadness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_solosis" index="643">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because their bodies are enveloped in\na special liquid, they are fine in any\nenvironment, no matter how severe.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_duosion" index="644">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When their two divided brains think the\nsame thoughts, their psychic power is\nmaximized.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_reuniclus" index="645">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They use psychic power to control their\narms, which are made of a special liquid.\nThey can crush boulders psychically.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_ducklett" index="646">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They are better at swimming than flying,\nand they happily eat their favorite food,\npeat moss, as they dive underwater.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_swanna" index="647">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Despite their elegant appearance,\nthey can flap their wings strongly\nand fly for thousands of miles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_vanillite" index="648">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Theoretically, this Pokémon formed from\nicicles bathed in energy from the morning\nsun. Their breath is -58 degrees Farenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_vanillish" index="649">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They cool down the surrounding air\nand create ice particles, which\nthey use to freeze their foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_vanilluxe" index="650">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Swallowing large amounts of water, they\nmake snow clouds inside their bodies and,\nwhen angry, cause violent blizzards.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_deerling" index="651">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their coloring changes according to the\nseasons and can be slightly affected\nby the temperature and humidity as well.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sawsbuck" index="652">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They migrate according to the seasons,\nso some people call Sawsbuck the\nharbingers of spring.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_frillish" index="653">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If its veil-like arms stun and wrap\na foe, that foe will be dragged miles\nbelow the surface, never to return.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_jellicent" index="654">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is mostly seawater.\nIt’s said there’s a castle of ships\nJellicent have sunk on the seafloor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_alomomola" index="655">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gently holds injured\nand weak Pokémon in its fins.\nIts special membrane heals their wounds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tynamo" index="656">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">One alone can emit only a trickle of\nelectricity, so a group of them gathers\nto unleash a powerful electric shock.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_eelektrik" index="657">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It wraps itself around its prey and\nparalyzes it with electricity from the\nround spots on its sides. Then it chomps.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_eelektross" index="658">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It latches on to prey with its sucker mouth,\nsinking in its fangs and shocking the prey\nwith powerful electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_axew" index="659">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its large tusks have a tendency to break,\nbut each time they grow back, they grow\nin harder and sturdier.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_fraxure" index="660">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A broken tusk will not grow back,\nso it diligently sharpens its tusks on\nriver rocks after the end of a battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_haxorus" index="661">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its tusks are incredibly destructive.\nThey can easily slice through a thick,\nsturdy steel column every time.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cubchoo" index="662">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their snot is a barometer of health.\nWhen healthy, their snot is sticky and\nthe power of their ice moves increases.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_beartic" index="663">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They love the cold seas of the north.\nThey create pathways across the\nocean waters by freezing their own breath.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cryogonal" index="664">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They are composed of ice crystals.\nThey capture prey with chains of ice,\nfreezing the prey at -148 degrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_stunfisk" index="665">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its opponent can’t be paralyzed,\nit contorts itself with unexpected speed\nand flops away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_mienfoo" index="666">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It takes pride in the speed at which it\ncan use moves. What it loses in power,\nit makes up for in quantity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_mienshao" index="667">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Using the long fur on its arms like whips,\nit launches into combo attacks that,\nonce started, no one can stop.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_druddigon" index="668">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It runs through the narrow tunnels\nformed by Excadrill and Onix.\nIt uses its sharp claws to catch prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_golett" index="669">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ancient science fashioned\nthis Pokémon from clay.\nIt’s been active for thousands of years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_golurk" index="670">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Golurk were created to protect\npeople and Pokémon.\nThey run on a mysterious energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pawniard" index="671">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ignoring their injuries, groups attack\nby sinking the blades that cover\ntheir bodies into their prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_bisharp" index="672">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This pitiless Pokémon commands a group\nof Pawniard to hound prey into immobility.\nIt then moves in to finish the prey off.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_rufflet" index="673">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stands up to massive opponents, not\nout of courage, but out of recklessness.\nBut that is how it gets stronger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_braviary" index="674">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For the sake of its friends, this\nbrave warrior of the sky will not\nstop battling, even if injured.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_vullaby" index="675">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their wings are too tiny to allow them to fly.\nThey guard their posteriors with bones that\nwere gathered by Mandibuzz.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_mandibuzz" index="676">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They fly in circles around the sky.\nWhen they spot prey, they attack and\ncarry it back to their nest with ease.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_heatmor" index="677">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It draws in air through its tail, transforms\nit into fire, and uses it like a tongue.\nIt melts Durant and eats them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_durant" index="678">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Individuals each play different roles in\ndriving Heatmor, their natural predator,\naway from their colony.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_deino" index="679">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Lacking sight, it’s unaware of its\nsurroundings, so it bumps into\nthings and eats anything that moves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_zweilous" index="680">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The two heads do not get along.\nWhichever head eats more than\nthe other gets to be the leader.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_hydreigon" index="681">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It responds to movement by attacking.\nThis scary, three-headed Pokémon\ndevours everything in its path!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_larvesta" index="682">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Said to have been born from the sun,\nit spews fire from its horns and encases\nitself in a cocoon of fire when it evolves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_volcarona" index="683">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Thought to be an embodiment of the sun,\nit appeared during a bitterly cold winter\nand saved Pokémon from freezing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cobalion" index="684">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has a body and heart of steel.\nIt worked with its allies to punish\npeople when they hurt Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_terrakion" index="685">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Spoken of in legend, this Pokémon\nused its phenomenal power to destroy a\ncastle in its effort to protect Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_virizion" index="686">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Legends say this Pokémon\nconfounded opponents\nwith its swift movements.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tornadus" index="687">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In every direction it flies,\ncreating winds so powerful,\nthey blow everything away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_thundurus" index="688">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it flies around, it shoots lightning all\nover the place and causes forest fires.\nIt is therefore disliked.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_reshiram" index="689">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary Pokémon can scorch\nthe world with fire. It helps those\nwho want to build a world of truth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_zekrom" index="690">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary Pokémon can scorch\nthe world with lightning. It assists those\nwho want to build an ideal world.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_landorus" index="691">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">From the forces of lightning and wind,\nit creates energy to give nutrients\nto the soil and make the land abundant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_kyurem" index="692">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This legendary ice Pokémon waits for\na hero to fill in the missing parts\nof its body with truth or ideals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_keldeo" index="693">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it is resolute, its body fills\nwith power and it becomes swifter.\nIts jumps are then too fast to follow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_meloetta" index="694">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The melodies sung by Meloetta\nhave the power to make Pokémon\nthat hear them happy or sad.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_genesect" index="695">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon existed 300 million years ago.\nTeam Plasma altered it and attached\na cannon to its back.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_chespin" index="696">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Such a thick shell of wood covers its\nhead and back that even a direct hit\nfrom a truck wouldn’t faze it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_quilladin" index="697">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It relies on its sturdy shell to\ndeflect predators’ attacks. It\ncounterattacks with its sharp quills.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_chesnaught" index="698">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it takes a defensive posture with\nits fists guarding its face, it could\nwithstand a bomb blast.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_fennekin" index="699">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Eating a twig fills it with energy, and\nits roomy ears give vent to very hot\nair.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_braixen" index="700">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With friction from its tail fur, it\nsets the twig on its tail on fire and\nlaunches into battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_delphox" index="701">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gazes into the flame at its branch\nto achieve a focused state, allowing it\nto see the future.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_froakie" index="702">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It secretes bubbles from its chest and\nback. The bubbles reduce the damage it\nwould take when attacked.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_frogadier" index="703">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its swiftness is unparalleled. It can\nscale a tower of more than 2,000 feet in\na minute’s time.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_greninja" index="704">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It creates throwing stars out of\ncompressed water, that can split metal\nin two.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_scatterbug" index="705">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The powder that covers its body\nregulates its temperature, so it can\nlive in any region or climate.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_spewpa" index="706">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The beaks of birds can’t begin to\nscratch its stalwart body. To defend\nitself, it spews powder.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_vivillon" index="707">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The colorful patterns on this Pokémon’s\nwings depend on the climate and\ntopography of its habitat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_flabebe" index="708">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It draws and controls the hidden power\nof flowers. The flower it holds is most\nlikely part of its body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_floette" index="709">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the flowers of a well-tended\nflower bed bloom, it appears and\ncelebrates with an elegant dance.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_florges" index="710">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its life can span several hundred\nyears. It’s said to devote its entire\nlife to protecting gardens.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_skiddo" index="711">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Thought to be one of the first Pokémon\nto live in harmony with humans, it has\na placid disposition.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gogoat" index="712">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They inhabit mountainous regions. The\nleader of the herd is decided by a\nbattle of clashing horns.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pancham" index="713">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It grows up imitating the behavior of\nPangoro, which it looks up to as a\nleader.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pangoro" index="714">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon boasts great physical\nstrength. Many Trainers are also smitten\nby its lively character.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_furfrou" index="715">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Historically, in the Kalos region,\nthese Pokémon were the designated\nguardians of the king.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_honedge" index="716">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is born when a departed spirit\ninhabits a sword. It attaches to people\nand drinks their life force.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_doublade" index="717">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The complex attack patterns of its two\nswords are unstoppable, even for an\naccomplished opponent.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_aegislash" index="718">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can detect the innate qualities of\nleadership. Whoever it recognizes is\ndestined to become king.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_spritzee" index="719">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It emits a scent that delights those\nwho smell it. The fragrance changes\ndepending on what it has eaten.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_aromatisse" index="720">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It devises various scents and emits\nscents that its enemies dislike in order\nto gain an edge in battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_swirlix" index="721">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because it eats nothing but sweets, its\nfur is as sticky sweet as cotton\ncandy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_slurpuff" index="722">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can distinguish the faintest of\nscents. It puts its sense of smell to\nuse by helping pastry chefs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_inkay" index="723">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It draws prey near with its blinking\nlights and then wraps them up in its\nlong tentacles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_malamar" index="724">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It wields the most compelling hypnotic\npowers of any Pokémon, and it forces\nothers to do anything.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_binacle" index="725">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Two Binacle live together on one rock.\nWhen they fight, one of them will move\nto a different rock.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_barbaracle" index="726">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When they evolve, two Binacle multiply\ninto seven. They fight with the power\nof seven Binacle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_skrelp" index="727">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It looks just like rotten kelp. It\nhides from foes while storing up power\nfor its evolution.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dragalge" index="728">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Tales are told of ships that wander\ninto seas where Dragalge live, never to\nreturn.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_clauncher" index="729">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They knock down flying prey by firing\ncompressed water from their massive\nclaws like shooting a pistol.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_clawitzer" index="730">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Their enormous claws launch cannonballs\nof water powerful enough to pierce\ntanker hulls.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_helioptile" index="731">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The frills on either side of its head\nhave cells that generate electricity\nwhen exposed to sunlight.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_heliolisk" index="732">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flares its frill and generates\nenergy. It can generate sufficient\nelectricity to power a skyscraper.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tyrunt" index="733">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its immense jaws have enough destructive\nforce to chew up an automobile. It lived\n100 million years ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tyrantrum" index="734">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Nothing could stop this Pokémon 100\nmillion years ago, so it behaved like a\nking.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_amaura" index="735">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This calm Pokémon lived in a cold land\nwhere there were no violent predators\nlike Tyrantrum.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_aurorus" index="736">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This usually quiet and kindly Pokémon\nhas a surface temperature of around -240\ndegrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_hawlucha" index="737">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Although its body is small, its\nproficient fighting skills enable it to\nkeep up with big bruisers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_carbink" index="738">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Born from temperatures and pressures\ndeep underground, it fires beams from\nthe stone in its head.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_goomy" index="739">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s covered in a slimy membrane that\nmakes any punches or kicks slide off it\nharmlessly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sliggoo" index="740">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It crawls along sluggishly. The swirly\nprotrusion on its back is filled with\nits brain and other organs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_goodra" index="741">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An amazingly friendly Pokémon, but if\nleft to itself, loneliness overcomes it,\nand it oozes gooey tears.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_klefki" index="742">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These key collectors threaten any\nattackers by fiercely jingling their\nkeys at them.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_bergmite" index="743">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It blocks opponents’ attacks with the\nice that shields its body. It uses cold\nair to repair any crack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_avalugg" index="744">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The way several Bergmite huddle on its\nback make it look like an aircraft\ncarrier made of ice.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_xerneas" index="745">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the horns on its head shine in\nseven different colors, it is said to be\nsharing everlasting life.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_yveltal" index="746">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its life comes to an end, it\nabsorbs the life energy of every living\nthing and turns into a cocoon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_zygarde" index="747">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When the Kalos region’s ecosystem falls\ninto disarray, it appears and reveals\nits secret power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_diancie" index="748">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can instantly create many diamonds\nby compressing the carbon in the air\nbetween its hands.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_hoopa" index="749">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gathers things it likes and passes\nthem through its loop to teleport them\nto a secret place.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_volcanion" index="750">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It expels its internal steam from the\narms on its back. It has enough power to\nblow away a mountain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_rowlet" index="751">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It feels relaxed in tight, dark places\nand has been known to use its Trainer’s\npocket or bag as a nest.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dartrix" index="752">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It throws sharp feathers called blade\nquills at enemies or prey. It seldom\nmisses.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_decidueye" index="753">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Although basically cool and cautious,\nwhen it’s caught by surprise, it’s\nseized by panic.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_litten" index="754">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It doesn’t allow its emotions to be\neasily seen. Earning its trust takes\ntime. It prefers solitude.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_torracat" index="755">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It boasts powerful front legs. With a\nsingle punch, it can bend an iron bar\nright over.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_incineroar" index="756">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When its fighting spirit is set alight,\nthe flames around its waist become\nespecially intense.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_popplio" index="757">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The balloons it inflates with its nose\ngrow larger and larger as it practices\nday by day.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_brionne" index="758">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attacks by smacking its enemies with\nthe exploding water balloons that it\ncreates.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_primarina" index="759">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To Primarina, every battle is a stage.\nIt takes down its prey with beautiful\nsinging and dancing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pikipek" index="760">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It may look spindly, but its neck\nmuscles are heavy-duty. It can peck at a\ntree 16 times per second!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_trumbeak" index="761">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can bend the tip of its beak to\nproduce over a hundred different cries\nat will.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_toucannon" index="762">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Known for forming harmonious couples,\nit is brought to wedding ceremonies as a\ngood luck charm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_yungoos" index="763">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It prefers to eat fresh living things\nso it marches down streets in search of\nprey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gumshoos" index="764">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Patient by nature, it loses control of\nitself and pounces when it spots its\nfavorite meal-Rattata!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_grubbin" index="765">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its strong jaw enables it to scrape\ntrees and slurp out the sap. It normally\nlives underground.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_charjabug" index="766">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">From the food it digests, it generates\nelectricity, and it stores this energy\nin its electric sac.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_vikavolt" index="767">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It flusters opponents with acrobatic\nflying maneuvers. This creates an\nopening for it to attack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_crabrawler" index="768">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its hard pincers are well suited to\nboth offense and defense.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_crabominable" index="769">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stores coldness in its pincers and\npummels its foes. It can even smash\nthick walls of ice to bits!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_oricorio" index="770">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Oricorio has sipped red nectar. Its\npassionate dance moves cause its enemies\nto combust in both body and mind.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cutiefly" index="771">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Myriads of Cutiefly flutter above the\nheads of people who have auras\nresembling those of flowers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_ribombee" index="772">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Some of Ribombee’s pollen puffs are\nhighly nutritious. They are sometimes\nsold as supplements.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_rockruff" index="773">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it rubs the rocks on its neck\nagainst you, that’s proof of its love\nfor you.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_lycanroc" index="774">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Well equipped with claws and fangs, it\nuses the sharp rocks in its mane as\nweapons.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_wishiwashi" index="775">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They’re weak, so they move in schools.\nHowever, they can also often be seen all\nalone, having strayed from the school.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_mareanie" index="776">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Aside from its head, its body parts\nregenerate quickly if they’re cut off.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_toxapex" index="777">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It crawls along the ocean floor on its\n12 legs. It leaves a trail of Corsola\nbits scattered in its wake.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_mudbray" index="778">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The mud stuck to Mudbray’s hooves\nenhances its grip and its powerful\nrunning gait.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_mudsdale" index="779">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can trudge mountain roads without\nrest for three days, all the while\ndragging a 10-ton load.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dewpider" index="780">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It crawls onto the land in search of\nfood. Its water bubble allows it to\nbreathe and protects its head.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_araquanid" index="781">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It delivers headbutts with the bubble\non its head. Small Pokémon get sucked\ninto it, where they drown.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_fomantis" index="782">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It loves the sunshine. When it basks in\nthe sunlight regularly, it grows up\nwith vivid coloration.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_lurantis" index="783">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">For self-protection, it pretends to be\na bug Pokémon. Both of its arms bear\nkeen-edged petals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_morelull" index="784">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It scatters spores that flicker and\nglow. Anyone seeing these lights falls\ninto a deep slumber.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_shiinotic" index="785">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it starts fighting for territory\nwith Parasect, the entire area gets\ncompletely coated in spores!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_salandit" index="786">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It burns its bodily fluids to create a\npoisonous gas. It weakens enemies and\nsends them reeling with it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_salazzle" index="787">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It punishes Salandit that couldn’t\nbring it food with a fierce slap of its\nflame-spewing palm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_stufful" index="788">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Stufful hates to be hugged or touched\nin any way. It will squirm, thrash, and\nresist with amazing power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_bewear" index="789">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It boasts tremendous physical strength.\nMany people call it the most dangerous\nPokémon in Alola region.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_bounsweet" index="790">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because of its sweet, delicious aroma,\nbird Pokémon are always after it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_steenee" index="791">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It bounces around, swinging the sepals\non its head with abandon. It’s quite\npainful when it smacks you!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tsareena" index="792">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A master of grand and beautiful kicks,\nit can knock out even kickboxing\nchampions with a single blow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_comfey" index="793">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Baths prepared with the flowers from\nits vine have a relaxing effect so it is\na hit to many people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_oranguru" index="794">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Known for its extreme intelligence, it\nwill look down on inexperienced\nTrainers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_passimian" index="795">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They form groups of 20 individuals.\nTheir mutual bond is remarkable-they\nwill never let down a comrade.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_wimpod" index="796">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An astonishingly coward Pokémon, it\nwhirs its legs at high speed to run away\nif anything comes near it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_golisopod" index="797">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With a flashing slash of its giant\nsharp claws, it cleaves seawater-or even\nair-right in two.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sandygast" index="798">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Born from a sand mound playfully built\nby a child, this Pokémon embodies the\ngrudges of the departed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_palossand" index="799">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Buried beneath the castle are masses of\ndried-up bones from those whose\nvitality it has drained.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pyukumuku" index="800">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is covered with slime. If you\naccidentally step on it, you’ll slip,\nand it will get mad at you!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_type_null" index="801">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">There’s danger of its going on a\nrampage, so its true power is sealed\naway beneath its control mask.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_silvally" index="802">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It destroyed its own control mask. It\nhas become capable of changing type by\nequipping special memories.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_minior" index="803">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It eats dust in the atmosphere. The\ncomposition of the dust determines the\ncolor of its core.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_komala" index="804">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stays asleep from the moment it’s\nborn. When it falls into a deep sleep,\nit stops moving altogether.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_turtonator" index="805">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gushes fire and poisonous gases from\nits nostrils. Its dung is an explosive\nsubstance.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_togedemaru" index="806">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it’s surprised or agitated, the 14\nfur spikes on its back will stand up\ninvoluntarily.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_mimikyu" index="807">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It conceals its terrifying appearance\nbeneath an old rag so it can get closer\nto people and Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_bruxish" index="808">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its skin is thick enough to fend off\nspikes. With its robust teeth, it\ncrunches up and eats the spikes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_drampa" index="809">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It appears in towns and plays with the\nchildren. Drampa will protect kids when\nthey’re in danger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dhelmise" index="810">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It wraps its prey in green seaweed and\nsucks away their vitality. It only\nlikes to go after big prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_jangmo_o" index="811">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They live in mountains where no trace\nof humans can be detected. It grows as\nit battles others.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_hakamo_o" index="812">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It leaps at its prey with a courageous\nshout. Its scaly punches tear its\nopponents to shreds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_kommo_o" index="813">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It battles valiantly with its fists,\nwhich are armored in steel scales.\nKommo-o specializes in uppercuts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tapu_koko" index="814">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This guardian deity of Melemele summons\nthunderclouds and stores their\nlightning inside its body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tapu_lele" index="815">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This guardian deity of Akala is\nguilelessly cruel. Its flowers’ fragrant\naroma is its source of energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tapu_bulu" index="816">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The guardian deity of Ula’ula is a lazy\nPokémon. It commands plants to\nimmobilize its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tapu_fini" index="817">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The guardian deity of Poni can control\nwater. It can create pure water that\nwill wash away any impurity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cosmog" index="818">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is gaseous and frail. It\nslowly grows as it collects dust from\nthe atmosphere.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cosmoem" index="819">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it absorbs light, Cosmoem continues\nto grow. Its golden shell is\nsurprisingly solid.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_solgaleo" index="820">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">In writings from the distant past, it’s\ncalled by the name ’the beast that\ndevours the sun.’.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_lunala" index="821">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sometimes summons unknown powers and\nlife-forms to this world from holes\nthat lead to other worlds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_nihilego" index="822">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A life-form from another world, it was\ndubbed a UB and is thought to produce a\nstrong neurotoxin.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_buzzwole" index="823">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Buzzwole goes around showing off its\nabnormally swollen muscles. It is one\nkind of Ultra Beast.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pheromosa" index="824">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">One of the dangerous Ultra Beasts, it\nhas been spotted running across the land\nat terrific speeds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_xurkitree" index="825">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole. It\nraided a power plant, so it energizes\nitself with electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_celesteela" index="826">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole.\nWitnesses observed it flying across the\nsky at high speed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_kartana" index="827">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Ultra Beast’s body, which is as\nthin as paper, is like a sharpened\nsword.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_guzzlord" index="828">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An unknown life-form called a UB. It\nmay be constantly hungry-it is certainly\nalways devouring something.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_necrozma" index="829">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Light is the source of its energy. If\nit isn’t devouring light, impurities\nbuild up in it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_magearna" index="830">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its mechanized body is merely a vessel.\nIts true self is its Soul-Heart, an\nartificial soul.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_marshadow" index="831">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lurks in the shadows of others,\ncopying their movements and powers. It\nis craven and cowering.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_poipole" index="832">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Ultra Beast is well enough liked\nto be chosen as a first partner in its\nown world.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_naganadel" index="833">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It stores hundreds of liters of\npoisonous liquid in its body. It is one\nof the organisms known as UBs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_stakataka" index="834">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When stone walls started moving and\nattacking, the brute’s true identity was\nthis mysterious life-form.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_blacephalon" index="835">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It causes explosions, then takes\nadvantage of opponents’ surprise to rob\nthem of their vitality.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_zeraora" index="836">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It approaches its enemies at the speed\nof lightning, then tears them limb from\nlimb with its sharp claws.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_meltan" index="837">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It melts particles of iron and other\nmetals found in the subsoil, so it can\nabsorb theminto its body of molten steel.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_melmetal" index="838">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Revered long ago for its capacity to\ncreate iron from nothing, for some reason\nit has come back to life after 3,000 years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_grookey" index="839">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It attacks with rapid beats of its\nstick. As it strikes with amazing speed,\nit gets more and more pumped.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_thwackey" index="840">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The faster a Thwackey can beat out a\nrhythm with its two sticks, the more respect\nit wins from its peers.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_rillaboom" index="841">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By drumming, it taps into the power of\nits special tree stump. The roots of the\nstump follow its direction in battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_scorbunny" index="842">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has special pads on the backs of\nits feet, and one on its nose. Its\npads radiate tremendous heat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_raboot" index="843">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its thick and fluffy fur protects it\nfrom the cold and enables it to\nuse hotter fire moves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cinderace" index="844">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It gets pumped up when cheered on.\nBut if it starts showboating, it could put\nitself in a tough spot.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sobble" index="845">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it gets wet, its skin changes\ncolor, and this Pokémon becomes\ninvisible as if it were camouflaged.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_drizzile" index="846">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Highly intelligent but also very lazy,\nit keeps enemies out of its territory\nby laying traps everywhere.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_inteleon" index="847">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It picks out foes’ weak points so it\ncan precisely blast them with water\nthat shoots from its fingertips.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_skwovet" index="848">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon becomes uneasy if its\ncheeks are ever completely empty\nof berries.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_greedent" index="849">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon has strong teeth and\ncan chew through the toughest of\nberry shells.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_rookidee" index="850">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It will bravely challenge any foe, no\nmatter how powerful. Even suffering\na defeat increases its strength a bit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_corvisquire" index="851">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The lessons of many harsh battles\nhave taught it how to accurately judge\nan opponent’s strength.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_corviknight" index="852">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The black luster of its steel body\ncould drive terror into the heart of\nany foe.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_blipbug" index="853">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A constant collector of information,\nthis Pokémon is very smart. Very\nstrong is what it isn’t.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dottler" index="854">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it grows inside its shell, it uses\nits psychic abilities to monitor its\nsurroundings and wait for evolution.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_orbeetle" index="855">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s famous for its high intelligence,\nand the large size of its brain is proof\nthat it has immense psychic power.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_nickit" index="856">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Aided by the soft pads on its feet, it\nsilently raids the food stores of others.\nIt survives off its ill-gotten gains.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_thievul" index="857">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With a lithe body and sharp claws, it\ngoes around stealing food and eggs.\nIt secretly marks its future targets.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gossifleur" index="858">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It anchors itself in the ground and\nbasks in the sun. After absorbing\nenough sunlight, it blooms vividly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_eldegoss" index="859">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The seeds attached to its cotton fluff\nare full of nutrients. It spreads them on\nthe wind so that others can benefit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_wooloo" index="860">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If its fleece grows too long, it won’t\nbe able to move. Cloth made with\nits wool is surprisingly durable.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dubwool" index="861">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its majestic horns are meant only to\nimpress the opposite gender. They\nnever see use in battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_chewtle" index="862">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Apparently the itch of its teething\nimpels it to snap its jaws at anything\nin front of it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_drednaw" index="863">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With jaws that can shear through steel\nrods, this highly aggressive Pokémon\nchomps down on its unfortunate prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_yamper" index="864">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This greedy Pokémon only helps people\nwith their work because it wants treats.\nAs it runs, it crackles with electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_boltund" index="865">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sends electricity through its legs\nto boost their strength. Running at\ntop speed, it easily breaks 50 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_rolycoly" index="866">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can race around like a unicycle,\neven on rough, rocky terrain. Burning\ncoal sustains it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_carkol" index="867">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">By rapidly rolling its legs, it can\neasily travel at over 18 mph. It\nforms coal inside its body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_coalossal" index="868">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">While engaged in battle, its mountain\nof coal will burn bright red, scorching\nthe surrounding area with sparks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_silicobra" index="869">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It spews sand from its nostrils. While\nthe enemy is blinded, it burrows into\nthe ground to hide.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sandaconda" index="870">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it contracts its body, over 220\npounds of sand sprays from its nose.\nIt becomes disheartened if it runs out.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cramorant" index="871">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This hungry Pokémon swallows Arrokuda\nwhole. Occasionally, it makes a mistake\nand tries to swallow other Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_arrokuda" index="872">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It becomes extremely sluggish after\neating its fill. That’s when Cramorant\nswallows it up.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_barraskewda" index="873">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its jaw that’s as sharp as a spear and\nas strong as steel. It spins its tail fins\nto surge forward at over 100 knots.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_toxel" index="874">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It manipulates the chemical makeup of\nits poison to produce electricity. Despite\na weak voltage, it can cause paralysis.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_toxtricity" index="875">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This short-tempered and aggressive\nPokémon chugs stagnant water to\nabsorb any toxins it might contain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_clobbopus" index="876">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s very curious, but its means of\ninvestigating things is to try to punch\nthem with its tentacles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_grapploct" index="877">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Searching for an opponent to test its\nskills against, it emerges onto land. Once\nthe battle is over, it returns to the sea.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sinistea" index="878">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon is said to have been\nborn when a lonely spirit possessed\na cold, leftover cup of tea.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_polteageist" index="879">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This species lives in antique teapots.\nMost pots are forgeries, but on rare\noccasions, an authentic work is found.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_hatenna" index="880">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Via the protrusion on its head, it\nsenses other creatures’ emotions.\nIt prefers areas without people.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_hattrem" index="881">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">No matter who you are, if you bring\nstrong emotions near this Pokémon,\nit will silence you violently.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_hatterene" index="882">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Known as the Forest Witch, if you are\ntoo loud around it, you risk being torn\napart by the claws on its tentacle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_impidimp" index="883">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It sneaks into people’s homes, taking\nand feasting on the negative energy\nof the frustrated occupants.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_morgrem" index="884">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With sly cunning, it lures people into\nthe woods. Some believe it to have\nthe power to make crops grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_grimmsnarl" index="885">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its hairs work like muscle fibers.\nWhen its hairs unfurl, they latch on to\nfoes, ensnaring them like tentacles.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_obstagoon" index="886">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It evolved after experiencing numerous\nfights. While crossing its arms, it lets out a\nshout that would make anyone flinch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_perrserker" index="887">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">What appears to be an iron helmet is\nactually hardened hair. This Pokémon\nlives for the thrill of battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cursola" index="888">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Be cautious of the ectoplasmic body\nsurrounding its soul. You’ll become stiff\nas stone if you touch it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sirfetchd" index="889">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">After deflecting attacks with its hard\nleaf shield, it strikes back with its sharp\nleek stalk. </language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_mr_rime" index="890">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its amusing movements make it very\npopular. It releases its psychic power\nfrom the pattern on its belly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_runerigus" index="891">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Never touch its shadowlike body, or\nyou’ll be shown the horrific memories\nbehind the picture carved into it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_milcery" index="892">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They say that any patisserie visited\nby Milcery is guaranteed success and\ngood fortune.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_alcremie" index="893">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It evolved from a Milcery that held\nonto a Strawberry Sweet. Its flavor\ndepends on how it was mixed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_falinks" index="894">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The six of them work together as one.\nTeamwork is also their battle strategy, and\nthey constantly change their formation.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pincurchin" index="895">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It feeds on seaweed, using its teeth\nto scrape it off rocks. Electric current\nflows from the tips of its spines.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_snom" index="896">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It eats snow that piles up on the\nground. The more snow it eats, the\nbigger its spikes grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_frosmoth" index="897">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Icy scales fall from its wings\nlike snow as it flies over fields\nand mountains.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_stonjourner" index="898">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Once a year, on a specific date and\nat a specific time, they gather out of\nnowhere and form up in a circle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_eiscue" index="899">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It drifted in on the flow of ocean\nwaters from a frigid place. It keeps its\nhead iced constantly to stay cold.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_indeedee" index="900">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Through its horns, it can pick up on\nthe emotions of creatures around it. Males\nwill act as valets for those they serve.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_morpeko" index="901">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it eats the seeds stored up in its\npouches, it generates electricity while\nsatisfying its constant hunger.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cufant" index="902">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If a job requires serious strength,\nCufant will excel at it. Its copper body\ntarnishes in the rain, turning green.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_copperajah" index="903">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon live in herds. Their\ntrunks have incredible grip strength,\nstrong enough to crush giant rocks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dracozolt" index="904">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The powerful muscles in its tail\ngenerate its electricity. Its upper half\nis entirely too small. </language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_arctozolt" index="905">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The shaking of its freezing upper half\nis what generates its electricity. It has\na hard time walking around.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dracovish" index="906">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its mighty legs are capable of running\nat speeds exceeding 40 mph, but it can’t\nbreathe unless it’s underwater.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_arctovish" index="907">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The skin on its face is impervious\nto attack, but breathing difficulties\nmade it go extinct anyway.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_duraludon" index="908">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body resembles polished metal,\nand it’s both lightweight and strong.\nHowever, its body rusts easily.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dreepy" index="909">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">After being reborn as a ghost, Dreepy\nwanders the areas it used to inhabit back\nwhen it was alive in prehistoric seas.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_drakloak" index="910">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s capable of flying faster than 120\nmph. It battles alongside Dreepy and\ndotes on them until they evolve.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dragapult" index="911">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Apparently the Dreepy inside its horns\neagerly look forward to being launched\nout at Mach speeds.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_zacian" index="912">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It  has slumbered for many years. Some\nsay it is Zamazenta’s elder sister,\nothers say the two are rivals.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_zamazenta" index="913">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It slept for aeons while in the form\nof a statue. It was asleep for so long,\npeople forgot that it ever existed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_eternatus" index="914">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It was inside a meteorite that fell\n20,000 years ago. The energy that\nits core absorbs allows it to live.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_kubfu" index="915">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">If it pulls the long white hair on\nits head, its fighting spirit heightens and\npower wells up from deep in its belly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_urshifu" index="916">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Inhabiting the mountains of a distant\nregion, it races across sheer cliffs, training\nits legs and refining its moves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_zarude" index="917">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Once the vines on its body tear off,\nthey become nutrients in the soil. This helps\nthe plants of the forest grow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_regieleki" index="918">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its entire body is made of an organ\nthat generates electricity. It is capable of\ngenerating a region’s worth of electricity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_regidrago" index="919">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body is composed of crystallized\ndragon energy. It is said to contain the\npower of every Dragon Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_glastrier" index="920">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Glastrier has tremendous physical\nstrength. The mask covering its face is\n100 times stronger than diamond.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_spectrier" index="921">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">As it dashes through the night, it\nabsorbs the life energy of sleeping Pokémon. It\ncraves silence and solitude.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_calyrex" index="922">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its every move is filled with grace\nand dignity. Extremely intelligent, it is said\nto see past, present, and future events.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_basculegion" index="923">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon is cloaked in the souls of its\ncomrades who perished during a punishing\njourney to the river of their birth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sneasler" index="924">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Because of Sneasler’s virulent poison and\ndaunting physical prowess, no other species\ncould hope to best it on the frozen highlands.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_overqwil" index="925">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Overqwil’s poisonous spikes will reflexively\nreact even while Overqwil sleeps, stabbing\nany moving thing that approaches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_enamorus" index="926">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When it flies to this land from across the sea, the bitter winter\ncomes to an end. According to legend, this Pokémon’s love\ngives rise to the budding of fresh life across Hisui.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sprigatito" index="927">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The sweet scent its body gives off\nmesmerizes those around it. The scent grows\nstronger when this Pokémon is in the sun.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_floragato" index="928">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Floragato deftly wields the vine hidden\nbeneath its long fur, slamming the hard\nflower bud against its opponents.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_meowscarada" index="929">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">With skillful misdirection, it rigs foes with\npollen-packed flower bombs, and sets them\noff before its foes realize what’s going on.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_fuecoco" index="930">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lies on warm rocks and uses the\nheat absorbed by its square-shaped\nscales to create fire energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_crocalor" index="931">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The combination of Crocalor’s fire energy\nand overflowing vitality has caused an\negg-shaped fireball to appear on its head.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_skeledirge" index="932">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Skeledirge’s gentle singing soothes the souls of all that hear it. It burns its enemies to a crisp with flames of over 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_quaxly" index="933">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its strong legs let it easily swim around in\neven fast-flowing rivers. It likes to keep\nthings tidy and is prone to overthinking.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_quaxwell" index="934">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The hardworking Quaxwell observes people and Pokémon from various regions and incorporates their movements into its own dance routines.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_quaquaval" index="935">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Dancing in ways that evoke far-away places, this Pokémon mesmerizes all that see it. Flourishes of its decorative water feathers slice into its foes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_lechonk" index="936">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon spurns all but the finest\nof foods. Its body gives off an herblike\nscent that bug Pokémon detest.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_oinkologne" index="937">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Oinkologne is proud of its fine,\nglossy skin. It emits a concentrated\nscent from the tip of its tail.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tarountula" index="938">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The ball of threads wrapped around its body\nis elastic enough to deflect the scythes of\nScyther, this Pokémon’s natural enemy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_spidops" index="939">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It clings to branches and ceilings using its\nthreads and moves without a sound. It takes\nout its prey before the prey even notices it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_nymble" index="940">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has its third set of legs folded up. When\nit’s in a tough spot, this Pokémon jumps\nover 30 feet using the strength of its legs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_lokix" index="941">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It uses its normally folded third set of legs when in Showdown Mode. This places a huge burden on its body, so it can’t stay in this mode for long.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pawmi" index="942">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The pads of its paws are electricity-discharging organs. Pawmi fires electricity from its forepaws while standing unsteadily on its hind legs.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pawmo" index="943">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Pawmo uses a unique fighting technique in which it uses its forepaws to strike foes and zap them with electricity from its paw pads simultaneously.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pawmot" index="944">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Pawmot’s fluffy fur acts as a battery.\nIt can store the same amount of\nelectricity as an electric car.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tandemaus" index="945">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The pair sticks together no matter what.\nThey split any food they find exactly\nin half and then eat it together.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_maushold" index="946">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The two little ones just appeared one day.\nThe group might be a family of related\nPokémon, but nobody knows for sure.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_fidough" index="947">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The yeast in Fidough’s breath is useful\nfor cooking, so this Pokémon has been\nprotected by people since long ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dachsbun" index="948">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The surface of this Pokémon’s skin\nhardens when exposed to intense heat,\nand its body has an appetizing aroma.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_smoliv" index="949">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon converts nutrients into oil, which it stores in the fruit on its head. It can easily go a whole week without eating or drinking.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dolliv" index="950">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Dolliv shares its tasty, fresh-scented oil\nwith others. This species has coexisted\nwith humans since times long gone.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_arboliva" index="951">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This calm Pokémon is very compassionate.\nIt will share its delicious, nutrient-rich\noil with weakened Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_squawkabilly" index="952">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon prefer to live in cities.\nThey form flocks based on the color of\ntheir feathers, and they fight over territory.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_nacli" index="953">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The ground scrapes its body as it travels, causing it to leave salt behind. Salt is constantly being created and replenished inside Nacli’s body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_naclstack" index="954">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It compresses rock salt inside its body and shoots out hardened salt pellets with enough force to perforate an iron sheet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_garganacl" index="955">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Garganacl will rub its fingertips together\nand sprinkle injured Pokémon with salt. Even\nsevere wounds will promptly heal afterward.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_charcadet" index="956">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its firepower increases when it fights,\nreaching over 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit.\nIt likes berries that are rich in fat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_armarouge" index="957">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Armarouge evolved through the use of a set\nof armor that belonged to a distinguished\nwarrior. This Pokémon is incredibly loyal.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_ceruledge" index="958">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An old set of armor steeped in grudges\ncaused this Pokémon’s evolution. Ceruledge\ncuts its enemies to pieces without mercy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tadbulb" index="959">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Tadbulb shakes its tail to generate\nelectricity. If it senses danger, it will make\nits head blink on and off to alert its allies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_bellibolt" index="960">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">What appear to be eyeballs are actually\norgans for discharging the electricity\ngenerated by Bellibolt’s belly-button dynamo.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_wattrel" index="961">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon make their nests on coastal\ncliffs. The nests have a strange, crackling\ntexture, and they’re a popular delicacy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_kilowattrel" index="962">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Kilowattrel inflates its throat sac to\namplify its electricity. By riding the wind,\nthis Pokémon can fly over 430 miles in a day.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_maschiff" index="963">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its well-developed jaw and fangs are strong\nenough to crunch through boulders, and its\nthick fat makes for an excellent defense.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_mabosstiff" index="964">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon can store energy in its\nlarge dewlap. Mabosstiff unleashes this\nenergy all at once to blow away enemies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_shroodle" index="965">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">To keep enemies away from its territory,\nit paints markings around its nest using\na poisonous liquid that has an acrid odor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_grafaiai" index="966">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Each Grafaiai paints its own individual\npattern, and it will paint that same pattern\nover and over again throughout its life.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_bramblin" index="967">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Not even Bramblin knows where it is headed\nas it tumbles across the wilderness, blown\nby the wind. It loathes getting wet.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_brambleghast" index="968">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Brambleghast wanders around arid regions.\nOn rare occasions, mass outbreaks of\nthese Pokémon will bury an entire town.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_toedscool" index="969">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Though it looks like Tentacool, Toedscool is\na completely different species. Its legs may\nbe thin, but it can run at a speed of 30 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_toedscruel" index="970">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon gather into groups and\nform colonies deep within forests. They\nabsolutely hate it when strangers approach.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_klawf" index="971">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon lives on sheer cliffs.\nIt sidesteps opponents’ attacks, then\nlunges for their weak spots with its claws.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_capsakid" index="972">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The more sunlight this Pokémon bathes in,\nthe more spicy chemicals are produced by its\nbody, and thus the spicier its moves become.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_scovillain" index="973">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The red head converts spicy chemicals into\nfire energy and blasts the surrounding area\nwith a super spicy stream of flame.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_rellor" index="974">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It rolls its mud ball around while the energy\nit needs for evolution matures.\nEventually the time comes for it to evolve.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_rabsca" index="975">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The body that supports the ball barely moves.\nTherefore, it is thought that the true body\nof this Pokémon is actually inside the ball.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_flittle" index="976">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It spends its time running around wastelands.\nIf anyone steals its beloved berries, it will\nchase them down and exact its revenge.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_espathra" index="977">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It emits psychic power from the gaps\nbetween its multicolored frills and\nsprints at speeds greater than 120 mph.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tinkatink" index="978">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It swings its handmade hammer around to\nprotect itself, but the hammer is often\nstolen by Pokémon that eat metal.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tinkatuff" index="979">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These Pokémon make their homes in piles of\nscrap metal. They test the strength of each\nother’s hammers by smashing them together.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tinkaton" index="980">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This intelligent Pokémon has a very daring\ndisposition. It knocks rocks into the sky with\nits hammer, aiming for flying Corviknight.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_wiglett" index="981">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon can pick up the scent\nof a Veluza just over 65 feet away\nand will hide itself in the sand.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_wugtrio" index="982">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A variety of fish Pokémon,\nWugtrio was once considered\nto be a regional form of Dugtrio.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_bombirdier" index="983">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Bombirdier uses the apron on its chest to bundle up food, which it carries back to its nest. It enjoys dropping things that make loud noises.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_finizen" index="984">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its water ring is made from seawater\nmixed with a sticky fluid that Finizen\nsecretes from its blowhole.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_palafin" index="985">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its physical capabilities are no different\nthan a Finizen’s, but when its allies are in\ndanger, it transforms and powers itself up.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_varoom" index="986">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The steel section is Varoom’s actual body. This Pokémon clings to rocks and converts the minerals within into energy to fuel its activities.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_revavroom" index="987">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It creates a gas out of poison and minerals\nfrom rocks. It then detonates the gas\nin its eight cylinders to generate energy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cyclizar" index="988">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It can sprint at over 70 mph while carrying a\nhuman. The rider’s body heat warms Cyclizar’s\nback and lifts the Pokémon’s spirit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_orthworm" index="989">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When attacked, this Pokémon will wield\nthe tendrils on its body like fists and pelt\nthe opponent with a storm of punches.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_glimmet" index="990">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It absorbs nutrients from cave walls.\nThe petals it wears are made of\ncrystallized poison.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_glimmora" index="991">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When this Pokémon detects danger,\nit will open up its crystalline petals\nand fire beams from its conical body.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_greavard" index="992">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is said that a dog Pokémon that died\nin the wild without ever interacting with\na human was reborn as this Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_houndstone" index="993">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Houndstone spends most of its time sleeping\nin graveyards. Among all the dog Pokémon,\nthis one is most loyal to its master.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_flamigo" index="994">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon apparently ties the base of its\nneck into a knot so that the energy stored\nin its belly does not escape from its beak.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cetoddle" index="995">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives in frigid regions in pods of\nfive or so individuals. It loves the\nminerals found in snow and ice.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_cetitan" index="996">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ice energy builds up in the horn on its upper\njaw, causing the horn to reach cryogenic\ntemperatures that freeze its surroundings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_veluza" index="997">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Veluza has excellent regenerative capabilities. It sheds spare flesh from its body to boost its agility, then charges at its prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_dondozo" index="998">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon is a glutton,\nbut it’s bad at getting food.\nIt teams up with a Tatsugiri to catch prey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_tatsugiri" index="999">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This is a small dragon Pokémon.\nIt lives inside the mouth of Dondozo to\nprotect itself from enemies on the outside.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_clodsire" index="1000">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives at the bottom of ponds and swamps.\nIt will carry Wooper on its back and ferry\nthem across water from shore to shore.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_kingambit" index="1001">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Only a Bisharp that stands above all\nothers in its vast army can evolve\ninto Kingambit.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_great_tusk" index="1002">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This creature resembles a mysterious\nPokémon that, according to a paranormal\nmagazine, has lived since ancient times.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_scream_tail" index="1003">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It resembles a mysterious Pokémon\ndescribed in a paranormal magazine as a\nJigglypuff from one billion years ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_brute_bonnet" index="1004">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It bears a slight resemblance to a Pokémon\ndescribed in a dubious magazine as a cross\nbetween a dinosaur and a mushroom.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_flutter_mane" index="1005">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has similar features to a ghostly pterosaur\nthat was covered in a paranormal magazine,\nbut the two have little else in common.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_slither_wing" index="1006">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon somewhat resembles an\nancient form of Volcarona that was\nintroduced in a dubious magazine.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sandy_shocks" index="1007">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It slightly resembles a Magneton that\nlived for 10,000 years and was featured in\nan article in a paranormal magazine.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_iron_treads" index="1008">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon closely resembles a scientific\nweapon that a paranormal magazine claimed\nwas sent to this planet by aliens.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_iron_bundle" index="1009">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its shape is similar to a robot featured in a\nparanormal magazine. The robot was said to\nhave been created by an ancient civilization.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_iron_hands" index="1010">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It is very similar to a cyborg covered by a\nparanormal magazine. The cyborg was said to\nbe the modified form of a certain athlete.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_iron_jugulis" index="1011">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s possible that Iron Jugulis,\nan object described in an old book,\nmay actually be this Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_iron_moth" index="1012">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon resembles an unknown object\ndescribed in a paranormal magazine\nas a UFO sent to observe humanity.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_iron_thorns" index="1013">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has some similarities to a Pokémon\nintroduced in a dubious magazine as a\nTyranitar from 1 billion years in the future.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_frigibax" index="1014">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon lives in forests and crags.\nUsing the power of its dorsal fin, it cools\nthe inside of its nest like a refrigerator.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_arctibax" index="1015">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Arctibax freezes the air around it,\nprotecting its face with an ice mask and\nturning its dorsal fin into a blade of ice.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_baxcalibur" index="1016">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon blasts cryogenic air\nout from its mouth. This air can\ninstantly freeze even liquid-hot lava.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gimmighoul" index="1017">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It lives inside an old treasure chest.\nSometimes it gets left in shop corners since\nno one realizes it’s actually a Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gholdengo" index="1018">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its body seems to be made up of 1,000 coins.\nThis Pokémon gets along well with others\nand is quick to make friends with anybody.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_wo_chien" index="1019">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It drains the life-force from vegetation,\ncausing nearby forests to instantly wither\nand fields to turn barren.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_chien_pao" index="1020">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon can control 100 tons of fallen\nsnow. It plays around innocently by leaping\nin and out of avalanches it has caused.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_ting_lu" index="1021">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The fear poured into an ancient ritual\nvessel has clad itself in rocks and\ndirt to become a Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_chi_yu" index="1022">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The envy accumulated within curved beads\nthat sparked multiple conflicts has clad\nitself in fire and become a Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_roaring_moon" index="1023">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">According to a dubious magazine,\nthis Pokémon has some connection to a\nphenomenon that occurs in a certain region.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_iron_valiant" index="1024">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It has some similarities to a\nmad scientist’s invention\ncovered in a paranormal magazine.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_koraidon" index="1025">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This Pokémon resembles Cyclizar, but it is\nfar burlier and more ferocious. Nothing is\nknown about its ecology or other features.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_miraidon" index="1026">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Much remains unknown about this\ncreature. It resembles Cyclizar, but\nit is far more ruthless and powerful.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_walking_wake" index="1027">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It resembles an illustration published in\na paranormal magazine, said to be a\ndepiction of a super-ancient Suicune.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_iron_leaves" index="1028">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Many of its physical characteristics match\nthose of a Virizion from the future that\nwas covered in a paranormal magazine.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_poltchageist" index="1029">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Poltchageist looks like a regional form of\nSinistea, but it was recently discovered\nthat the two Pokémon are entirely unrelated.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_sinistcha" index="1030">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It pretends to be tea, trying to fool people\ninto drinking it so it can drain their life-\nforce. Its ruse is generally unsuccessful.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_okidogi" index="1031">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Okidogi is a ruffian with a short temper.\nIt can pulverize anything by swinging\naround the chain on its neck.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_munkidori" index="1032">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Munkidori keeps itself somewhere safe\nwhile it toys with its foes, using\npsychokinesis to induce intense dizziness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_fezandipiti" index="1033">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Fezandipiti beats its glossy wings to\nscatter pheromones that captivate\npeople and Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_ogerpon" index="1034">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This mischief-loving Pokémon is full of\ncuriosity. It battles by drawing out the type-\nbased energy contained within its masks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_archaludon" index="1035">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It digs holes on mountains, searching\nfor food. It’s so durable that being\ncaught in a cave-in won’t faze it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_gouging_fire" index="1036">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It resembles a Pokémon once shown in a\nparanormal magazine. That Pokémon was said\nto be an Entei regenerated from a fossil.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_raging_bolt" index="1037">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It bears resemblance to a Pokémon that\nbecame a hot topic for a short while after\nbeing touted it as Raikou’s ancestor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_iron_boulder" index="1038">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It resembles a Pokémon described in a\ndubious magazine as a Terrakion that had\nbeen modified by an evil organization.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_iron_crown" index="1039">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It resembles a mysterious object introduced\nin a paranormal magazine as a cutting-edge\nweapon shaped like a Cobalion.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_terapagos" index="1040">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s thought that this Pokémon lived\nin ancient Paldea until it got caught\nin seismic shifts and went extinct.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0803_pecharunt" index="1041">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Its peach-shaped shell serves as storage\nfor a potent poison. It makes poisonous\nmochi and serves it to people and Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
</body>
